    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-restore-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 50
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit_restore (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit_restore AS

                    TYPE t_names IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(128) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;
                    TYPE t_seen  IS TABLE OF BOOLEAN INDEX BY VARCHAR2(64);

                    -- Child events that had to wait for another parent row (restore_row)
                    g_pending t_names;

                    FUNCTION q(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN '"' || p_name || '"';
                    END;

                    FUNCTION pk_columns(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN t_names IS
                        l_cols t_names;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT cols.column_name
                        BULK COLLECT INTO l_cols
                        FROM user_constraints cons
                        JOIN user_cons_columns cols
                          ON cols.constraint_name = cons.constraint_name
                        WHERE cons.table_name = p_table_name
                          AND cons.constraint_type = 'P'
                        ORDER BY cols.position;
                        RETURN l_cols;
                    END;

                    -- PK value in the same format the trigger writes to PK_VALUE_VC
                    FUNCTION pk_string(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2, p_row IN json_object_t) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_cols t_names := pk_columns(p_table_name);
                        l_obj  json_object_t := json_object_t();
                    BEGIN
                        IF l_cols.COUNT = 1 THEN
                            RETURN p_row.get_string(l_cols(1));
                        END IF;
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_cols.COUNT LOOP
                            l_obj.put(l_cols(i), p_row.get_string(l_cols(i)));
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l_obj.to_string;
                    END;

                    -- SQL expression that turns a stored text value back into the column's
                    -- type. The inverse of util_audit_gen's to_char_expr; NLS-independent.
                    FUNCTION from_text_expr(p_bind IN VARCHAR2, p_data_type IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_dt VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(p_data_type);
                        c_greg CONSTANT VARCHAR2(40) := q'[, 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN')]';
                    BEGIN
                        IF v_dt IN ('NUMBER', 'FLOAT') THEN
                            RETURN 'JSON_VALUE(JSON_OBJECT(''v'' VALUE ' || p_bind || '), ''$.v'' RETURNING NUMBER ERROR ON ERROR)';
                        ELSIF v_dt IN ('BINARY_FLOAT', 'BINARY_DOUBLE') THEN
                            RETURN 'JSON_VALUE(JSON_OBJECT(''v'' VALUE ' || p_bind || '), ''$.v'' RETURNING BINARY_DOUBLE ERROR ON ERROR)';
                        ELSIF v_dt = 'RAW' THEN
                            RETURN 'HEXTORAW(' || p_bind || ')';
                        ELSIF v_dt = 'DATE' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_DATE(' || p_bind || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS']' || c_greg;
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP% TIME ZONE' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_TIMESTAMP_TZ(' || p_bind || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS.FF TZH:TZM']' || c_greg;
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP%' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_TIMESTAMP(' || p_bind || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS.FF']' || c_greg;
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'INTERVAL DAY%' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_DSINTERVAL(' || p_bind || ')';
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'INTERVAL YEAR%' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_YMINTERVAL(' || p_bind || ')';
                        ELSE
                            -- character types and CLOB
                            RETURN p_bind;
                        END IF;
                    END;

                    -- Equal as stored text, byte for byte (not affected by NLS_COMP)
                    FUNCTION same(p_a IN VARCHAR2, p_b IN VARCHAR2) RETURN BOOLEAN IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN p_a IS NOT NULL AND p_b IS NOT NULL
                           AND UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(p_a, 'AL32UTF8') = UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(p_b, 'AL32UTF8');
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE say(p_depth IN PLS_INTEGER, p_text IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD(' ', p_depth * 2) || p_text);
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE restore_event(
                        p_txn_id           IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_include_children IN BOOLEAN,
                        p_force            IN BOOLEAN,
                        p_depth            IN PLS_INTEGER,
                        p_seen             IN OUT NOCOPY t_seen
                    );

                    -- Restores child rows that went with a deleted parent row. A child event
                    -- belongs to the parent when it is in the same database transaction and
                    -- its old FK values equal the parent's old key values.
                    PROCEDURE restore_children(
                        p_parent    IN util_audit_txn%ROWTYPE,
                        p_old       IN json_object_t,
                        p_force     IN BOOLEAN,
                        p_depth     IN PLS_INTEGER,
                        p_seen      IN OUT NOCOPY t_seen
                    ) IS
                        l_child_cols  t_names;
                        l_parent_cols t_names;
                        l_child_old   json_object_t;
                        l_child_new   json_object_t;
                        l_match       BOOLEAN;
                        l_fk_nulled   BOOLEAN;
                    BEGIN
                        FOR fk IN (
                            SELECT ch.child_table, ch.constraint_name, ch.delete_rule, ch.child_audited
                            FROM v_util_audit_child_tables ch
                            WHERE ch.parent_table = p_parent.table_name
                            ORDER BY ch.child_table, ch.constraint_name
                        ) LOOP
                            IF fk.child_audited = 'N' THEN
                                say(p_depth + 1, 'WARNING: ' || fk.child_table || ' references ' || p_parent.table_name ||
                                             ' (' || fk.constraint_name || ', ON DELETE ' || fk.delete_rule ||
                                             ') but is not audited. Child rows removed with this row cannot be restored.');
                            END IF;

                            -- Child FK columns paired with the parent key columns they reference
                            SELECT cc.column_name, pc.column_name
                            BULK COLLECT INTO l_child_cols, l_parent_cols
                            FROM user_constraints c
                            JOIN user_cons_columns cc
                              ON cc.constraint_name = c.constraint_name
                            JOIN user_cons_columns pc
                              ON pc.constraint_name = c.r_constraint_name
                             AND pc.position        = cc.position
                            WHERE c.constraint_name = fk.constraint_name
                            ORDER BY cc.position;

                            FOR ev IN (
                                SELECT transaction_id, transaction_type, old_row_json, new_row_json
                                FROM util_audit_txn
                                WHERE table_name        = fk.child_table
                                  AND db_transaction_id = p_parent.db_transaction_id
                                  AND transaction_type IN ('DELETE', 'UPDATE')
                                  AND old_row_json IS NOT NULL
                                ORDER BY audit_ts
                            ) LOOP
                                l_child_old := json_object_t.parse(ev.old_row_json);
                                l_match     := TRUE;
                                l_fk_nulled := TRUE;

                                IF ev.transaction_type = 'UPDATE' THEN
                                    l_child_new := json_object_t.parse(ev.new_row_json);
                                END IF;

                                FOR i IN 1 .. l_child_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                    IF NOT p_old.has(l_parent_cols(i))
                                       OR NOT same(l_child_old.get_string(l_child_cols(i)), p_old.get_string(l_parent_cols(i))) THEN
                                        l_match := FALSE;
                                        EXIT;
                                    END IF;
                                    IF ev.transaction_type = 'UPDATE'
                                       AND l_child_new.get_string(l_child_cols(i)) IS NOT NULL THEN
                                        l_fk_nulled := FALSE;
                                    END IF;
                                END LOOP;

                                -- An UPDATE only belongs to the parent delete if it set the FK
                                -- to NULL (ON DELETE SET NULL). An UPDATE that moved the child
                                -- to another parent is a separate change.
                                IF l_match AND (ev.transaction_type = 'DELETE' OR l_fk_nulled) THEN
                                    restore_event(ev.transaction_id, TRUE, p_force, p_depth + 1, p_seen);
                                END IF;
                            END LOOP;
                        END LOOP;
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE restore_event(
                        p_txn_id           IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_include_children IN BOOLEAN,
                        p_force            IN BOOLEAN,
                        p_depth            IN PLS_INTEGER,
                        p_seen             IN OUT NOCOPY t_seen
                    ) IS
                        e          util_audit_txn%ROWTYPE;
                        l_old      json_object_t;
                        l_new      json_object_t;
                        l_pk_cols  t_names;
                        l_pk_after VARCHAR2(4000);
                        l_later    NUMBER;
                        l_cols     t_names;
                        l_dts      t_names;
                        l_n        PLS_INTEGER := 0;
                        l_list     VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_vals     VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_where    VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_missing  VARCHAR2(4000);
                        l_sql      VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_cur      INTEGER;
                        l_rows     INTEGER;
                        l_clob     CLOB;
                        l_pk_dt    VARCHAR2(128);
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_seen.EXISTS(p_txn_id) THEN
                            RETURN;
                        END IF;
                        p_seen(p_txn_id) := TRUE;

                        BEGIN
                            SELECT * INTO e FROM util_audit_txn WHERE transaction_id = p_txn_id;
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20010, 'Audit event not found: ' || p_txn_id);
                        END;

                        -- The table name comes from audit data, so check it names a table
                        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO l_later FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = e.table_name;
                        IF l_later = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20019, 'Table ' || e.table_name || ' of event ' || p_txn_id ||
                                                            ' no longer exists.');
                        END IF;

                        IF e.transaction_type = 'INSERT' THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20011, 'INSERT events cannot be restored (event ' || p_txn_id || ').');
                        END IF;
                        IF e.old_row_json IS NULL THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20012, 'Event ' || p_txn_id || ' has no row snapshot. ' ||
                                                            'Events copied from util_audit v1, or recorded before v2.2, cannot be restored.');
                        END IF;

                        l_old := json_object_t.parse(e.old_row_json);

                        -- Where the row stands right after this event, and whether anything
                        -- happened to it since
                        IF e.transaction_type = 'UPDATE' THEN
                            l_new      := json_object_t.parse(e.new_row_json);
                            l_pk_after := pk_string(e.table_name, l_new);
                        ELSE
                            l_pk_after := e.pk_value_vc;
                        END IF;

                        SELECT COUNT(*)
                        INTO l_later
                        FROM util_audit_txn
                        WHERE table_name  = e.table_name
                          AND pk_value_vc = l_pk_after
                          AND audit_ts    > e.audit_ts;

                        IF l_later > 0 AND NOT p_force THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20013, e.table_name || ' ' || l_pk_after || ' has ' || l_later ||
                                ' later audit event(s). Restoring would overwrite them. Pass p_force => TRUE to do it anyway.');
                        END IF;

                        -- Columns to write: those in the snapshot that can still be written
                        FOR c IN (
                            SELECT tc.column_name, tc.data_type, tc.virtual_column, tc.nullable, tc.default_length,
                                   NVL(ic.generation_type, '-') generation_type
                            FROM user_tab_cols tc
                            LEFT JOIN user_tab_identity_cols ic
                              ON ic.table_name  = tc.table_name
                             AND ic.column_name = tc.column_name
                            WHERE tc.table_name    = e.table_name
                              AND tc.hidden_column = 'NO'
                            ORDER BY tc.column_id
                        ) LOOP
                            IF c.virtual_column = 'YES' THEN
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;
                            IF NOT l_old.has(c.column_name) THEN
                                IF e.transaction_type = 'DELETE' THEN
                                    l_pk_cols := pk_columns(e.table_name);
                                    FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                        IF l_pk_cols(i) = c.column_name THEN
                                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20015, 'Key column ' || c.column_name ||
                                                ' is not in the audit snapshot, so the row cannot be re-inserted.');
                                        END IF;
                                    END LOOP;
                                    -- Typically an excluded column (a password, say)
                                    IF c.nullable = 'N' AND NVL(c.default_length, 0) = 0 AND c.generation_type = '-' THEN
                                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20009, e.table_name || '.' || c.column_name ||
                                            ' is not recorded (it is excluded from auditing, or was added later) and is ' ||
                                            'NOT NULL without a default, so the deleted row cannot be re-inserted.');
                                    END IF;
                                END IF;
                                l_missing := l_missing || ', ' || c.column_name;
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;
                            IF c.generation_type = 'ALWAYS' THEN
                                IF e.transaction_type = 'DELETE' THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20014, e.table_name || '.' || c.column_name ||
                                        ' is GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, so the row cannot be re-inserted with its original value.');
                                END IF;
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;

                            l_n := l_n + 1;
                            l_cols(l_n) := c.column_name;
                            l_dts(l_n)  := c.data_type;

                            IF e.transaction_type = 'DELETE' THEN
                                l_list := l_list || ', ' || q(c.column_name);
                                l_vals := l_vals || ', ' || from_text_expr(':b' || l_n, c.data_type);
                            ELSE
                                l_list := l_list || ', ' || q(c.column_name) || ' = ' || from_text_expr(':b' || l_n, c.data_type);
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        IF e.transaction_type = 'DELETE' THEN
                            l_sql := 'INSERT INTO ' || q(e.table_name) || ' (' || SUBSTR(l_list, 3) || ')' ||
                                     ' VALUES (' || SUBSTR(l_vals, 3) || ')';
                        ELSE
                            -- Find the row by its key as it was right after the event
                            l_pk_cols := pk_columns(e.table_name);
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                IF NOT l_new.has(l_pk_cols(i)) THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20015, 'Key column ' || l_pk_cols(i) || ' is not in the audit snapshot.');
                                END IF;
                                SELECT data_type
                                INTO l_pk_dt
                                FROM user_tab_columns
                                WHERE table_name  = e.table_name
                                  AND column_name = l_pk_cols(i);
                                l_where := l_where || ' AND ' || q(l_pk_cols(i)) || ' = ' ||
                                           from_text_expr(':k' || i, l_pk_dt);
                            END LOOP;
                            l_sql := 'UPDATE ' || q(e.table_name) || ' SET ' || SUBSTR(l_list, 3) ||
                                     ' WHERE ' || SUBSTR(l_where, 6);
                        END IF;

                        l_cur := DBMS_SQL.OPEN_CURSOR;
                        BEGIN
                            DBMS_SQL.PARSE(l_cur, l_sql, DBMS_SQL.NATIVE);

                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_n LOOP
                                IF l_dts(i) = 'CLOB' THEN
                                    -- JSON null must stay NULL, not become an empty CLOB
                                    l_clob := CASE WHEN NOT l_old.get(l_cols(i)).is_null THEN l_old.get_clob(l_cols(i)) END;
                                    DBMS_SQL.BIND_VARIABLE(l_cur, ':b' || i, l_clob);
                                ELSE
                                    DBMS_SQL.BIND_VARIABLE(l_cur, ':b' || i, l_old.get_string(l_cols(i)), 32767);
                                END IF;
                            END LOOP;

                            IF e.transaction_type = 'UPDATE' THEN
                                FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                    DBMS_SQL.BIND_VARIABLE(l_cur, ':k' || i, l_new.get_string(l_pk_cols(i)), 32767);
                                END LOOP;
                            END IF;

                            l_rows := DBMS_SQL.EXECUTE(l_cur);
                            DBMS_SQL.CLOSE_CURSOR(l_cur);
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                IF DBMS_SQL.IS_OPEN(l_cur) THEN
                                    DBMS_SQL.CLOSE_CURSOR(l_cur);
                                END IF;
                                IF SQLCODE = -1 THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20016, e.table_name || ' ' || l_pk_after ||
                                        ' already exists, so the deleted row cannot be re-inserted.');
                                ELSIF SQLCODE = -2291 AND p_depth > 0 THEN
                                    -- A child row that also references another deleted parent:
                                    -- try again once the other rows are back (see restore_row)
                                    p_seen.DELETE(p_txn_id);
                                    g_pending(g_pending.COUNT + 1) := p_txn_id;
                                    say(p_depth, 'Waiting: ' || e.table_name || ' ' || l_pk_after ||
                                                 ' also needs another parent row.');
                                    RETURN;
                                ELSIF SQLCODE = -2291 THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20017, 'The parent row of ' || e.table_name || ' ' || l_pk_after ||
                                        ' does not exist. Restore the parent row first.', TRUE);
                                END IF;
                                RAISE;
                        END;

                        IF e.transaction_type = 'UPDATE' AND l_rows = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20018, e.table_name || ' ' || l_pk_after ||
                                ' no longer exists. Restore its DELETE event instead.');
                        END IF;

                        say(p_depth, 'Restored ' || e.table_name || ' ' || e.pk_value_vc ||
                                     ' (undid ' || e.transaction_type || ' at ' ||
                                     TO_CHAR(e.audit_ts, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN') || ')');
                        IF l_missing IS NOT NULL THEN
                            say(p_depth, '  Not in the audit snapshot, left ' ||
                                         CASE e.transaction_type WHEN 'DELETE' THEN 'NULL/default' ELSE 'as they are' END ||
                                         ': ' || SUBSTR(l_missing, 3));
                        END IF;

                        IF e.transaction_type = 'DELETE' AND p_include_children THEN
                            restore_children(e, l_old, p_force, p_depth, p_seen);
                        END IF;
                    END restore_event;

                    PROCEDURE restore_row(
                        p_transaction_id   IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_include_children IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
                        p_force            IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
                        p_preview          IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
                    ) IS
                        l_seen     t_seen;
                        l_module   VARCHAR2(64);
                        l_action   VARCHAR2(64);
                        l_waiting  t_names;
                        l_progress BOOLEAN;
                    BEGIN
                        SAVEPOINT util_audit_restore;
                        g_pending.DELETE;

                        -- Tag the session so the restore's own audit events say what they are
                        DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.READ_MODULE(l_module, l_action);
                        DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.SET_ACTION('util_audit.restore_row ' || SUBSTR(p_transaction_id, 1, 40));

                        restore_event(p_transaction_id, p_include_children, p_force, 0, l_seen);

                        -- Retry child rows that waited for another parent row until a round
                        -- restores none of them
                        LOOP
                            EXIT WHEN g_pending.COUNT = 0;
                            l_waiting  := g_pending;
                            g_pending.DELETE;
                            l_progress := FALSE;
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_waiting.COUNT LOOP
                                IF NOT l_seen.EXISTS(l_waiting(i)) THEN
                                    restore_event(l_waiting(i), p_include_children, p_force, 1, l_seen);
                                    l_progress := l_progress OR l_seen.EXISTS(l_waiting(i));
                                END IF;
                            END LOOP;
                            IF NOT l_progress AND g_pending.COUNT > 0 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20017, 'Event ' || g_pending(1) || ' references a parent row ' ||
                                    'that this restore does not bring back. Restore that parent row first.');
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        IF p_preview THEN
                            ROLLBACK TO util_audit_restore;
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Preview only: all changes rolled back.');
                        END IF;

                        DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.SET_ACTION(l_action);
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            ROLLBACK TO util_audit_restore;
                            g_pending.DELETE;
                            DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.SET_ACTION(l_action);
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Restore failed: all changes rolled back.');
                            RAISE;
                    END restore_row;

                END util_audit_restore;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 60
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit AS

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- ENABLE TABLE
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE enable_table(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        MERGE INTO util_audit_config c
                        USING (SELECT UPPER(p_table_name) table_name FROM dual) src
                        ON (c.table_name = src.table_name)
                        WHEN MATCHED THEN
                            UPDATE SET enabled_flag = 'Y'
                        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
                            INSERT (table_name, enabled_flag, created_on, created_by)
                            VALUES (src.table_name, 'Y', SYSDATE, USER);
                    END;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- DISABLE TABLE
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE disable_table(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        UPDATE util_audit_config
                        SET enabled_flag = 'N'
                        WHERE table_name = UPPER(p_table_name);
                    END;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- CHECK IF TABLE ENABLED
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    FUNCTION table_enabled(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) RETURN BOOLEAN IS
                        v_flag CHAR(1);
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT enabled_flag
                        INTO v_flag
                        FROM util_audit_config
                        WHERE table_name = UPPER(p_table_name);

                        RETURN NVL(v_flag, 'N') = 'Y';
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
                            RETURN FALSE;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION table_enabled_sql(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) RETURN Varchar2
                        IS
                    BEGIN
                        IF table_enabled(p_table_name) THEN
                            RETURN 'Y';
                        ELSE
                            RETURN 'N';
                        END IF;
                    END;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- BUILD AUDIT CONTEXT (JSON)
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Who and where, without repeating what other columns already hold.
                    -- The user is in USERNAME, so it is not repeated here. Empty values are
                    -- skipped.
                    --   APEX: app_id, page_id, session_id, action, ip (the address that
                    --     connected to the web server) and forwarded_for (the X-Forwarded-For
                    --     header, set by proxies and load balancers; the client can fake it).
                    --     MODULE and CLIENT_IDENTIFIER only restate app/page and user:session,
                    --     and the session's IP/host/OS user are the web server's, the same on
                    --     every row, so they are left out.
                    --   Other sessions: module, client_id, action, ip, host, os_user.
                    FUNCTION get_audit_context
                        RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_ctx  json_object_t := json_object_t();
                        l_page VARCHAR2(30);
                        l_ip   VARCHAR2(4000);
                        l_fwd  VARCHAR2(4000);

                        PROCEDURE put(p_key IN VARCHAR2, p_value IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        BEGIN
                            IF p_value IS NOT NULL THEN
                                l_ctx.put(p_key, p_value);
                            END IF;
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        IF sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_ID') IS NOT NULL THEN
                            -- Dynamic, so the package compiles where APEX is not installed.
                            -- Separate blocks: a job or REST call has APEX but no CGI env.
                            BEGIN
                                EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin :page := apex_application.g_flow_step_id; end;'
                                    USING OUT l_page;
                            EXCEPTION
                                WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                    NULL;
                            END;
                            BEGIN
                                EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'[
                                    begin
                                        :ip  := owa_util.get_cgi_env('REMOTE_ADDR');
                                        :fwd := owa_util.get_cgi_env('HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR');
                                    end;]'
                                    USING OUT l_ip, OUT l_fwd;
                            EXCEPTION
                                WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                    NULL;
                            END;
                            put('app_id',        sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_ID'));
                            put('page_id',       l_page);
                            put('session_id',    sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_SESSION'));
                            put('action',        sys_context('USERENV', 'ACTION'));
                            put('ip',            l_ip);
                            put('forwarded_for', l_fwd);
                        ELSE
                            put('module',     sys_context('USERENV', 'MODULE'));
                            put('client_id',  sys_context('USERENV', 'CLIENT_IDENTIFIER'));
                            put('action',     sys_context('USERENV', 'ACTION'));
                            put('ip',         sys_context('USERENV', 'IP_ADDRESS'));
                            put('host',       sys_context('USERENV', 'HOST'));
                            put('os_user',    sys_context('USERENV', 'OS_USER'));
                        END IF;

                        RETURN l_ctx.to_clob;
                    END;
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- CAPTURE AUDIT
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE capture_audit(
                        p_transaction_json IN json_object_t
                    ) IS
                        -- Longest value prefix fed to the change hash. 990 chars stays under
                        -- the 4000-byte SQL limit even at 4 bytes per character.
                        c_hash_chars CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 990;

                        TYPE t_vc   IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(4000) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;
                        TYPE t_clob IS TABLE OF CLOB INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;

                        -- util_audit v1 triggers send trans_type instead of transaction_type,
                        -- no row snapshots, and every column on every update
                        l_v1       BOOLEAN := NOT p_transaction_json.has('transaction_type')
                                              AND p_transaction_json.has('trans_type');
                        l_txn_id   util_audit_txn.transaction_id%TYPE   := NVL(p_transaction_json.get_string('transaction_id'),
                                                                               RAWTOHEX(SYS_GUID()));
                        l_table    util_audit_txn.table_name%TYPE       := p_transaction_json.get_string('table_name');
                        l_pk       util_audit_txn.pk_value_vc%TYPE      := p_transaction_json.get_string('pk_value');
                        l_type     util_audit_txn.transaction_type%TYPE := NVL(p_transaction_json.get_string('transaction_type'),
                                                                               p_transaction_json.get_string('trans_type'));
                        l_user     util_audit_txn.username%TYPE         := p_transaction_json.get_string('user_name');
                        l_cols     json_array_t                         := p_transaction_json.get_array('columns');
                        l_col      json_object_t;
                        l_val      VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_db_txn   util_audit_txn.db_transaction_id%TYPE := dbms_transaction.local_transaction_id;
                        l_context  CLOB := get_audit_context;
                        l_old_row  CLOB;
                        l_new_row  CLOB;
                        l_n        PLS_INTEGER := 0;

                        l_col_name t_vc;
                        l_dt       t_vc;
                        l_old_vc   t_vc;
                        l_new_vc   t_vc;
                        l_old_clob t_clob;
                        l_new_clob t_clob;
                        l_old_h    t_vc;
                        l_new_h    t_vc;
                        l_pk_h     VARCHAR2(4000) := SUBSTR(l_pk, 1, c_hash_chars);

                        -- Non-CLOB values go to the VARCHAR2 column when they fit in 4000
                        -- bytes, otherwise to the CLOB column.
                        PROCEDURE split_value(
                            p_key  IN VARCHAR2,
                            p_i    IN PLS_INTEGER,
                            p_vc   IN OUT NOCOPY t_vc,
                            p_clob IN OUT NOCOPY t_clob,
                            p_hash IN OUT NOCOPY t_vc
                        ) IS
                        BEGIN
                            p_vc(p_i)   := NULL;
                            p_clob(p_i) := NULL;

                            IF l_dt(p_i) = 'CLOB' THEN
                                -- get_clob turns a JSON null into the text 'null'
                                IF l_col.has(p_key) AND NOT l_col.get(p_key).is_null THEN
                                    p_clob(p_i) := l_col.get_clob(p_key);
                                END IF;
                                p_hash(p_i) := DBMS_LOB.SUBSTR(p_clob(p_i), c_hash_chars, 1);
                            ELSE
                                l_val := l_col.get_string(p_key);
                                IF LENGTHB(l_val) > 4000 THEN
                                    p_clob(p_i) := TO_CLOB(l_val);
                                ELSE
                                    p_vc(p_i) := l_val;
                                END IF;
                                p_hash(p_i) := SUBSTR(l_val, 1, c_hash_chars);
                            END IF;
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_transaction_json.get_object('old_row') IS NOT NULL THEN
                            l_old_row := p_transaction_json.get_object('old_row').to_clob;
                        END IF;
                        IF p_transaction_json.get_object('new_row') IS NOT NULL THEN
                            l_new_row := p_transaction_json.get_object('new_row').to_clob;
                        END IF;

                        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                        -- 1) The changed columns
                        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                        FOR i IN 0 .. l_cols.get_size - 1 LOOP
                            l_col := TREAT(l_cols.get(i) AS json_object_t);
                            l_n   := l_n + 1;
                            l_col_name(l_n) := l_col.get_string('column_name');
                            l_dt(l_n)       := NVL(l_col.get_string('data_type'), l_col.get_string('datatype'));
                            split_value('old_value', l_n, l_old_vc, l_old_clob, l_old_h);
                            split_value('new_value', l_n, l_new_vc, l_new_clob, l_new_h);

                            -- v1 sends unchanged columns too; keep only real changes, as v1 did
                            IF l_v1 AND (
                                   (l_old_vc(l_n) IS NULL AND l_new_vc(l_n) IS NULL
                                    AND l_old_clob(l_n) IS NULL AND l_new_clob(l_n) IS NULL)
                                -- Compared as bytes, so a case-only change counts under
                                -- a linguistic NLS_COMP
                                OR UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(l_old_vc(l_n), 'AL32UTF8')
                                   = UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(l_new_vc(l_n), 'AL32UTF8')
                                OR (l_old_clob(l_n) IS NOT NULL AND l_new_clob(l_n) IS NOT NULL
                                    AND DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(l_old_clob(l_n), l_new_clob(l_n)) = 0)) THEN
                                l_col_name.DELETE(l_n);
                                l_n := l_n - 1;
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        -- A v1 update that changed nothing records nothing, as in v1
                        IF l_v1 AND l_n = 0 THEN
                            RETURN;
                        END IF;

                        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                        -- 2) Header row, one per audited row event
                        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                        INSERT INTO util_audit_txn
                        (transaction_id,
                         db_transaction_id,
                         table_name,
                         pk_value_vc,
                         transaction_type,
                         username,
                         audit_context,
                         old_row_json,
                         new_row_json,
                         audit_ts)
                        VALUES
                        (l_txn_id,
                         l_db_txn,
                         l_table,
                         l_pk,
                         l_type,
                         l_user,
                         l_context,
                         l_old_row,
                         l_new_row,
                         SYSTIMESTAMP);


                        -- The hash covers table, column, PK and the first 990 chars of each
                        -- value. Each part is hashed on its own, so no input exceeds 4000 bytes
                        -- and parts cannot run into each other.
                        FORALL i IN INDICES OF l_col_name
                            INSERT INTO util_audit_records
                            (transaction_id,
                             table_name,
                             pk_value_vc,
                             transaction_type,
                             username,
                             column_name,
                             data_type,
                             old_value,
                             new_value,
                             old_clob,
                             new_clob,
                             change_hash,
                             audit_ts)
                            VALUES
                            (l_txn_id,
                             l_table,
                             l_pk,
                             l_type,
                             l_user,
                             l_col_name(i),
                             l_dt(i),
                             l_old_vc(i),
                             l_new_vc(i),
                             l_old_clob(i),
                             l_new_clob(i),
                             STANDARD_HASH(
                                 RAWTOHEX(STANDARD_HASH(l_table || CHR(31) || l_col_name(i), 'SHA256')) ||
                                 RAWTOHEX(STANDARD_HASH(l_pk_h, 'SHA256')) ||
                                 RAWTOHEX(STANDARD_HASH(l_old_h(i), 'SHA256')) ||
                                 RAWTOHEX(STANDARD_HASH(l_new_h(i), 'SHA256')),
                                 'SHA256'),
                             SYSTIMESTAMP);

                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            -- Triggers cannot use savepoints, so remove a half-written event
                            -- by hand before passing the error on.
                            DELETE FROM util_audit_records WHERE transaction_id = l_txn_id;
                            DELETE FROM util_audit_txn     WHERE transaction_id = l_txn_id;
                            RAISE;
                    END capture_audit;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- LOG ERROR
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE log_error(
                        p_table_name       IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_transaction_type IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_pk_value         IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_error_code       IN NUMBER,
                        p_error_message    IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_error_backtrace  IN VARCHAR2
                    ) IS
                        PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;
                    BEGIN
                        INSERT INTO util_audit_errors
                        (table_name,
                         transaction_type,
                         pk_value_vc,
                         username,
                         error_code,
                         error_message,
                         error_backtrace)
                        VALUES
                        (SUBSTR(p_table_name, 1, 255),
                         SUBSTR(p_transaction_type, 1, 6),
                         SUBSTRB(p_pk_value, 1, 4000),
                         SUBSTR(NVL(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), USER), 1, 255),
                         p_error_code,
                         SUBSTRB(p_error_message, 1, 4000),
                         SUBSTRB(p_error_backtrace, 1, 4000));
                        COMMIT;
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            ROLLBACK;
                    END log_error;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- PURGE
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE purge(
                        p_before         IN  TIMESTAMP,
                        p_table_name     IN  VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_events_deleted OUT NUMBER
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        DELETE FROM util_audit_records r
                        WHERE r.transaction_id IN (
                            SELECT t.transaction_id
                            FROM util_audit_txn t
                            WHERE t.audit_ts < p_before
                              AND (p_table_name IS NULL OR t.table_name = UPPER(p_table_name)));

                        DELETE FROM util_audit_txn t
                        WHERE t.audit_ts < p_before
                          AND (p_table_name IS NULL OR t.table_name = UPPER(p_table_name));

                        p_events_deleted := SQL%ROWCOUNT;
                    END purge;

                    PROCEDURE purge_errors(
                        p_before         IN  TIMESTAMP,
                        p_errors_deleted OUT NUMBER
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        DELETE FROM util_audit_errors WHERE error_ts < p_before;
                        p_errors_deleted := SQL%ROWCOUNT;
                    END purge_errors;

                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- RESTORE (the work is in util_audit_restore)
                -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE restore_row(
                        p_transaction_id   IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_include_children IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
                        p_force            IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
                        p_preview          IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        util_audit_restore.restore_row(p_transaction_id, p_include_children, p_force, p_preview);
                    END restore_row;

                END util_audit;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-gen-spec (
        execution {
            sequence: 70
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package util_audit_gen (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE util_audit_gen AS
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- util_audit_gen
                    --
                    -- Trigger generator for util_audit (v2).
                    --
                    -- Generates a row-level AFTER INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE trigger that:
                    --   - Normalizes transaction_type via INSERTING/UPDATING/DELETING
                    --   - Skips all work when the table is disabled in util_audit_config
                    --   - Leaves ignored columns (standard set + configurable list) out of the
                    --     changes; they stay in the row snapshots
                    --   - Audits only supported datatypes
                    --   - Records only changed columns on UPDATE, and only non-NULL columns
                    --     on INSERT and DELETE
                    --   - Skips calling util_audit.capture_audit on an UPDATE that changed
                    --     no audited column
                    --   - Captures row snapshots (old_row/new_row) as JSON
                    --   - Logs audit failures to util_audit_errors instead of failing the DML
                    --
                    -- create_audit_trigger also prints (DBMS_OUTPUT) every child table that
                    -- references the table, and whether that child table is audited.
                    --
                    -- create_audit_trigger registers the table in util_audit_config if it is
                    -- not there yet. An existing enabled/disabled flag is left as it is.
                    --
                    -- Notes:
                    --   * Designed for "single-row" triggers (FOR EACH ROW).
                    --   * PK can be any datatype. A single-column PK is stored as its value
                    --     (numbers/dates/timestamps via TO_CHAR). A composite PK is stored as
                    --     a JSON object, e.g. {"ORDER_ID":"100","LINE_NO":"1"}.
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                    -- Generate or execute the trigger DDL
                    -- p_action: 'EXECUTE' or 'GENERATE'
                    PROCEDURE create_audit_trigger(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_action     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'EXECUTE'
                    );

                    -- Drop the trigger if it exists
                    PROCEDURE drop_audit_trigger(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_action     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'EXECUTE'
                    );

                    -- Set additional ignored columns for this session only
                    -- (comma-separated, case-insensitive). Applies to every table.
                    PROCEDURE set_ignored_columns(
                        p_columns IN VARCHAR2
                    );

                    -- Store the columns one table's trigger should skip (comma-separated,
                    -- case-insensitive) in util_audit_config. When p_regenerate is TRUE and
                    -- the table has an audit trigger, the trigger is re-created right away.
                    PROCEDURE set_table_ignored_columns(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns    IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_regenerate IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE
                    );

                    -- Store the columns one table's trigger must never record, not in the
                    -- column changes and not in the row snapshots: passwords, token hashes
                    -- and other secrets (comma-separated, case-insensitive). Ignored columns
                    -- are different: they stay in the snapshots so restore can bring them
                    -- back. A primary key column cannot be excluded.
                    -- p_regenerate:    re-create the trigger right away if the table has one
                    -- p_scrub_history: also remove these columns from history already
                    --                  recorded (see scrub_columns). Does not commit.
                    PROCEDURE set_table_excluded_columns(
                        p_table_name    IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns       IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_regenerate    IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
                        p_scrub_history IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
                    );

                    -- Removes columns from one table's recorded history: from the row
                    -- snapshots of every event and the column changes. Use it when a
                    -- secret was audited before it was excluded. Archive files already
                    -- made (util_audit_archive) are not changed. Does not commit.
                    PROCEDURE scrub_columns(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns    IN VARCHAR2
                    );

                    -- The CREATE TRIGGER statement create_audit_trigger would run
                    FUNCTION get_trigger_ddl(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                    -- Re-create every existing audit trigger, e.g. after an upgrade.
                    -- Tables that fail are reported (DBMS_OUTPUT) and skipped; the call then
                    -- raises ORA-20004 naming how many failed.
                    PROCEDURE recreate_all_triggers;

                END util_audit_gen;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-gen-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 80
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit_gen (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit_gen AS

                    g_ignored_columns VARCHAR2(32767);

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Helpers
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    FUNCTION norm_name(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN UPPER(TRIM(p_name));
                    END;

                    -- Quoted identifier, so mixed-case and reserved-word names compile
                    FUNCTION q(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN '"' || p_name || '"';
                    END;

                    -- Quoted string literal
                    FUNCTION lit(p_text IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN '''' || REPLACE(p_text, '''', '''''') || '''';
                    END;

                    -- The util_audit trigger already on the table, if any
                    FUNCTION current_trigger(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_table VARCHAR2(128) := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_name  VARCHAR2(128);
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT MIN(trigger_name) INTO v_name
                        FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                        WHERE table_name = v_table
                          AND (trigger_name LIKE 'AUD\_%' ESCAPE '\' OR trigger_name LIKE 'UA\_AUD\_%' ESCAPE '\');
                        RETURN v_name;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION base_trig_name(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_table VARCHAR2(128) := norm_name(p_table_name);
                    BEGIN
                        -- Names are limited to 128 bytes. Very long table names are cut and
                        -- given a hash suffix so two tables never share a trigger name.
                        IF LENGTHB(v_table) <= 124 THEN
                            RETURN 'AUD_' || v_table;
                        END IF;
                        RETURN 'AUD_' || SUBSTRB(v_table, 1, 114) || '_' ||
                               TO_CHAR(DBMS_UTILITY.GET_HASH_VALUE(v_table, 0, 2147483647), 'FM0XXXXXXX');
                    END;

                    -- The name for the table's trigger: the one it already has, else
                    -- AUD_<table>, else UA_AUD_<table> when AUD_<table> belongs to someone
                    -- else's trigger
                    FUNCTION trig_name(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_current VARCHAR2(128) := current_trigger(p_table_name);
                        v_base    VARCHAR2(128) := base_trig_name(p_table_name);
                        v_taken   NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        IF v_current IS NOT NULL
                           AND v_current IN (v_base, SUBSTRB('UA_' || v_base, 1, 128)) THEN
                            RETURN v_current;
                        END IF;
                        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_taken FROM user_triggers WHERE trigger_name = v_base;
                        IF v_taken = 0 THEN
                            RETURN v_base;
                        END IF;
                        RETURN SUBSTRB('UA_' || v_base, 1, 128);
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE exec_sql(p_sql IN CLOB, p_action IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        IF norm_name(p_action) = 'GENERATE' THEN
                            -- Line by line: DBMS_OUTPUT cannot take more than 32K at once
                            DECLARE
                                l_pos PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                                l_nl  PLS_INTEGER;
                                l_len PLS_INTEGER := NVL(DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH(p_sql), 0);
                            BEGIN
                                WHILE l_pos <= l_len LOOP
                                    l_nl := DBMS_LOB.INSTR(p_sql, CHR(10), l_pos);
                                    IF l_nl = 0 THEN
                                        l_nl := l_len + 1;
                                    END IF;
                                    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(DBMS_LOB.SUBSTR(p_sql, l_nl - l_pos, l_pos));
                                    l_pos := l_nl + 1;
                                END LOOP;
                            END;
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(CHR(10));
                            RETURN;
                        END IF;

                        EXECUTE IMMEDIATE p_sql;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION in_list(p_list IN VARCHAR2, p_item IN VARCHAR2) RETURN BOOLEAN IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN INSTR(',' || UPPER(REPLACE(NVL(p_list,''),' ','')) || ',',
                                     ',' || UPPER(TRIM(p_item)) || ',') > 0;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION is_ignored_column(p_col IN VARCHAR2, p_table_list IN VARCHAR2) RETURN BOOLEAN IS
                        v_col VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_col));
                    BEGIN
                        -- Who/when bookkeeping columns: changing only these records nothing
                        IF v_col IN (
                            'CREATED','CREATED_ON','CREATED_BY',
                            'UPDATED','UPDATED_ON','UPDATED_BY',
                            'MODIFIED','MODIFIED_ON','MODIFIED_BY'
                        ) THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        -- Per-table ignores from util_audit_config
                        IF p_table_list IS NOT NULL AND in_list(p_table_list, v_col) THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        -- Session-level ignores from set_ignored_columns
                        IF g_ignored_columns IS NOT NULL AND in_list(g_ignored_columns, v_col) THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        RETURN FALSE;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION supported_datatype(p_data_type IN VARCHAR2) RETURN BOOLEAN IS
                        v_dt VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_data_type));
                    BEGIN
                        IF v_dt IN ('NUMBER','FLOAT','BINARY_FLOAT','BINARY_DOUBLE',
                                    'VARCHAR2','CHAR','NCHAR','NVARCHAR2',
                                    'DATE','CLOB','RAW') THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        IF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP%' THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        IF v_dt LIKE 'INTERVAL %' THEN
                            RETURN TRUE;
                        END IF;

                        -- Exclusions: BLOB, LONG, XMLTYPE, object types, etc.
                        RETURN FALSE;
                    END;

                    -- Build an expression that returns a VARCHAR2 representation of a bind.
                    -- p_ref is the full bind reference, e.g. :NEW."AMOUNT".
                    -- Output does not depend on session NLS settings.
                    FUNCTION to_char_expr(p_ref IN VARCHAR2, p_data_type IN VARCHAR2)
                        RETURN VARCHAR2
                    IS
                        v_dt VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_data_type));
                    BEGIN
                        IF v_dt IN ('VARCHAR2','CHAR','NCHAR','NVARCHAR2','CLOB') THEN
                            -- CLOBs are put into the JSON as-is
                            RETURN p_ref;
                        ELSIF v_dt IN ('NUMBER','FLOAT','BINARY_FLOAT','BINARY_DOUBLE') THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(' || p_ref || q'[, 'TM9', 'NLS_NUMERIC_CHARACTERS=''.,''')]';
                        ELSIF v_dt = 'RAW' THEN
                            RETURN 'RAWTOHEX(' || p_ref || ')';
                        -- Dates always in the Gregorian calendar, whatever the session uses
                        ELSIF v_dt = 'DATE' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(' || p_ref || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN')]';
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP% WITH LOCAL TIME ZONE' THEN
                            -- TZH/TZM are not valid for LTZ; cast to keep the offset
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(CAST(' || p_ref || ' AS TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE)' ||
                                   q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS.FF TZH:TZM', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN')]';
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP% WITH TIME ZONE' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(' || p_ref || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS.FF TZH:TZM', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN')]';
                        ELSIF v_dt LIKE 'TIMESTAMP%' THEN
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(' || p_ref || q'[, 'YYYY-MM-DD"T"HH24:MI:SS.FF', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN')]';
                        ELSE
                            -- INTERVAL and anything else
                            RETURN 'TO_CHAR(' || p_ref || ')';
                        END IF;
                    END;

                    -- Comparison predicate that handles NULL properly.
                    FUNCTION changed_predicate(p_col IN VARCHAR2, p_data_type IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_dt VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_data_type));
                        v_new VARCHAR2(4000) := ':NEW.' || q(p_col);
                        v_old VARCHAR2(4000) := ':OLD.' || q(p_col);
                    BEGIN
                        -- For LOBs, direct != is not allowed; use DBMS_LOB.COMPARE and NULL checks.
                        IF v_dt = 'CLOB' THEN
                            RETURN '(' ||
                                   '(' || v_new || ' IS NULL AND ' || v_old || ' IS NOT NULL)' ||
                                   ' OR (' || v_new || ' IS NOT NULL AND ' || v_old || ' IS NULL)' ||
                                   ' OR (' || v_new || ' IS NOT NULL AND ' || v_old || ' IS NOT NULL AND ' ||
                                         'DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(' || v_new || ',' || v_old || ') != 0)' ||
                                   ')';
                        END IF;

                        -- Character values compare as bytes: with NLS_COMP=LINGUISTIC a plain
                        -- != would miss changes such as 'smith' -> 'Smith'
                        IF v_dt IN ('VARCHAR2','CHAR','NCHAR','NVARCHAR2') THEN
                            v_new := 'UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(' || v_new || ', ''AL32UTF8'')';
                            v_old := 'UTL_I18N.STRING_TO_RAW(' || v_old || ', ''AL32UTF8'')';
                        END IF;

                        RETURN '(' ||
                               '(' || v_new || ' != ' || v_old || ')' ||
                               ' OR (' || v_new || ' IS NULL AND ' || v_old || ' IS NOT NULL)' ||
                               ' OR (' || v_new || ' IS NOT NULL AND ' || v_old || ' IS NULL)' ||
                               ')';
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE set_ignored_columns(p_columns IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        g_ignored_columns := p_columns;
                    END;

                    -- Prints the tables that reference p_table_name through a foreign key.
                    -- util_audit.restore_row can only bring back child rows from audited
                    -- child tables, so this shows the gaps up front.
                    PROCEDURE report_child_tables(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        v_found BOOLEAN := FALSE;
                    BEGIN
                        FOR fk IN (
                            SELECT child_table, constraint_name, delete_rule, child_audited
                            FROM v_util_audit_child_tables
                            WHERE parent_table = p_table_name
                            ORDER BY child_table, constraint_name
                        ) LOOP
                            IF NOT v_found THEN
                                DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Child tables of ' || p_table_name || ':');
                                v_found := TRUE;
                            END IF;
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('  ' || fk.child_table || ' (' || fk.constraint_name ||
                                                 ', ON DELETE ' || fk.delete_rule || '): ' ||
                                CASE WHEN fk.child_audited = 'Y' THEN 'audited'
                                     ELSE 'NOT audited, so util_audit.restore_row cannot bring back its rows. ' ||
                                          'Audit ' || fk.child_table || ' too to include it.'
                                END);
                        END LOOP;

                        IF NOT v_found THEN
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No child tables reference ' || p_table_name || '.');
                        END IF;
                    END;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Drop trigger
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE drop_audit_trigger(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_action     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'EXECUTE'
                    ) IS
                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128) := norm_name(p_table_name);
                    BEGIN
                        -- Every trigger on this table that calls util_audit, and no other
                        FOR t IN (
                            SELECT trigger_name
                            FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name
                        ) LOOP
                            exec_sql('DROP TRIGGER ' || q(t.trigger_name), p_action);
                        END LOOP;
                    END;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Trigger DDL
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    FUNCTION get_trigger_ddl(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        TYPE t_names IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(128) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;

                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128) := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_trg_name   VARCHAR2(128) := trig_name(p_table_name);
                        v_table_lit  VARCHAR2(512) := lit(v_table_name);

                        v_pk_cols    t_names;
                        v_pk_dts     t_names;
                        v_ignored    util_audit_config.ignored_columns%TYPE;
                        v_excluded   util_audit_config.excluded_columns%TYPE;
                        v_track      BOOLEAN;

                        v_sql        CLOB;
                        v_has_cols   BOOLEAN := FALSE;

                        -- local utility to append
                        PROCEDURE ap(p IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        BEGIN
                            v_sql := v_sql || p || CHR(10);
                        END;

                        -- :NEW value on INSERT, :OLD value otherwise
                        FUNCTION pk_part(p_col IN VARCHAR2, p_dt IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        BEGIN
                            RETURN 'CASE WHEN INSERTING THEN ' || to_char_expr(':NEW.' || q(p_col), p_dt) ||
                                   ' ELSE ' || to_char_expr(':OLD.' || q(p_col), p_dt) || ' END';
                        END;

                    BEGIN
                        -- Validate table exists
                        DECLARE
                            v_cnt NUMBER;
                        BEGIN
                            SELECT COUNT(*)
                            INTO v_cnt
                            FROM user_tables
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name;

                            IF v_cnt = 0 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20001, 'Table not found in schema: ' || v_table_name);
                            END IF;
                            -- Auditing the audit tables would recurse
                            IF v_table_name LIKE 'UTIL\_AUDIT\_%' ESCAPE '\' THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20005, 'util_audit''s own tables cannot be audited: ' || v_table_name);
                            END IF;
                        END;

                        -- Primary key columns and datatypes, in key order
                        SELECT cols.column_name, tc.data_type
                        BULK COLLECT INTO v_pk_cols, v_pk_dts
                        FROM user_constraints cons
                        JOIN user_cons_columns cols
                          ON cons.constraint_name = cols.constraint_name
                         AND cons.owner          = cols.owner
                        JOIN user_tab_columns tc
                          ON tc.table_name  = cons.table_name
                         AND tc.column_name = cols.column_name
                        WHERE cons.table_name = v_table_name
                          AND cons.constraint_type = 'P'
                        ORDER BY cols.position;

                        IF v_pk_cols.COUNT = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20002, 'No primary key found for table: ' || v_table_name);
                        END IF;

                        BEGIN
                            SELECT ignored_columns, excluded_columns INTO v_ignored, v_excluded
                            FROM util_audit_config
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name;
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
                                v_ignored  := NULL;
                                v_excluded := NULL;
                        END;

                        v_sql := EMPTY_CLOB();

                        ap('CREATE OR REPLACE TRIGGER ' || q(v_trg_name));
                        ap('AFTER INSERT OR UPDATE OR DELETE ON ' || q(v_table_name));
                        ap('FOR EACH ROW');
                        IF v_excluded IS NOT NULL THEN
                            ap('-- Never recorded (excluded): ' || REPLACE(v_excluded, ',', ', '));
                        END IF;
                        ap('DECLARE');
                        ap('    l_txn_id    VARCHAR2(64) := RAWTOHEX(SYS_GUID());');
                        ap('    l_action    VARCHAR2(6);');
                        ap('    l_pk        VARCHAR2(4000);');
                        ap('    l_has_changes BOOLEAN := FALSE;');
                        ap('    v_audit_json JSON_OBJECT_T;');
                        ap('    v_cols_arr   JSON_ARRAY_T;');
                        ap('    v_col_obj    JSON_OBJECT_T;');
                        ap('    v_old_row    JSON_OBJECT_T;');
                        ap('    v_new_row    JSON_OBJECT_T;');
                        IF v_pk_cols.COUNT > 1 THEN
                            ap('    v_pk_obj     JSON_OBJECT_T;');
                        END IF;
                        ap('    l_err_code  NUMBER;');
                        ap('    l_err_msg   VARCHAR2(4000);');
                        ap('    l_err_trace VARCHAR2(4000);');
                        ap('');
                        ap('    -- Last resort when util_audit itself cannot log: write the error');
                        ap('    -- straight to UTIL_AUDIT_ERRORS in its own transaction');
                        ap('    PROCEDURE log_direct IS');
                        ap('        PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;');
                        ap('    BEGIN');
                        ap('        INSERT INTO util_audit_errors');
                        ap('            (table_name, transaction_type, pk_value_vc, username, error_code, error_message, error_backtrace)');
                        ap('        VALUES (' || v_table_lit || ', l_action, SUBSTRB(l_pk, 1, 4000),');
                        ap('            SUBSTR(NVL(sys_context(''APEX$SESSION'', ''APP_USER''), USER), 1, 255),');
                        ap('            l_err_code, l_err_msg, l_err_trace);');
                        ap('        COMMIT;');
                        ap('    EXCEPTION');
                        ap('        WHEN OTHERS THEN');
                        ap('            ROLLBACK;');
                        ap('    END;');
                        ap('BEGIN');
                        ap('    -- Normalize transaction type (do NOT rely on ORA_SYSEVENT)');
                        ap('    l_action := CASE');
                        ap('        WHEN INSERTING THEN ''INSERT''');
                        ap('        WHEN UPDATING  THEN ''UPDATE''');
                        ap('        WHEN DELETING  THEN ''DELETE''');
                        ap('    END;');
                        ap('');
                        ap('    -- Skip when auditing is disabled in util_audit_config');
                        ap('    IF NOT util_audit.table_enabled(' || v_table_lit || ') THEN');
                        ap('        RETURN;');
                        ap('    END IF;');
                        ap('');

                        -- pk_value serialization
                        ap('    -- Primary key value');
                        IF v_pk_cols.COUNT = 1 THEN
                            ap('    l_pk := ' || pk_part(v_pk_cols(1), v_pk_dts(1)) || ';');
                        ELSE
                            ap('    v_pk_obj := JSON_OBJECT_T();');
                            FOR i IN 1 .. v_pk_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                ap('    v_pk_obj.put(' || lit(v_pk_cols(i)) || ', ' || pk_part(v_pk_cols(i), v_pk_dts(i)) || ');');
                            END LOOP;
                            ap('    l_pk := v_pk_obj.to_string;');
                        END IF;
                        ap('');

                        ap('    v_audit_json := JSON_OBJECT_T();');
                        ap('    v_cols_arr   := JSON_ARRAY_T();');
                        ap('    v_old_row    := JSON_OBJECT_T();');
                        ap('    v_new_row    := JSON_OBJECT_T();');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''pk_value'', l_pk);');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''transaction_id'', l_txn_id);');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''table_name'', ' || v_table_lit || ');');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''transaction_type'', l_action);');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''user_name'', NVL(sys_context(''APEX$SESSION'',''APP_USER''), USER));');
                        ap('');

                        -- Per column: row snapshots and column-level changes
                        -- (supported columns only, excluding ignored)
                        FOR c IN (
                            SELECT column_name, data_type
                            FROM user_tab_columns
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name
                            ORDER BY column_id
                        ) LOOP
                            IF NOT supported_datatype(c.data_type) THEN
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;
                            -- Excluded columns are never read: not in the changes, not in
                            -- the snapshots
                            IF v_excluded IS NOT NULL AND in_list(v_excluded, c.column_name) THEN
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;
                            -- Ignored columns are left out of the changes but kept in the row
                            -- snapshots: restore needs the whole row (e.g. a NOT NULL CREATED)
                            v_track := NOT is_ignored_column(c.column_name, v_ignored);

                            ap('    -- ' || c.column_name);
                            IF UPPER(c.data_type) = 'CLOB' THEN
                                -- An unchanged CLOB is left out of UPDATE snapshots; restore
                                -- then leaves it as it is
                                ap('    IF DELETING OR (UPDATING AND ' || changed_predicate(c.column_name, c.data_type) || ') THEN');
                                ap('        v_old_row.put(' || lit(c.column_name) || ', :OLD.' || q(c.column_name) || ');');
                                ap('    END IF;');
                                ap('    IF INSERTING OR (UPDATING AND ' || changed_predicate(c.column_name, c.data_type) || ') THEN');
                                ap('        v_new_row.put(' || lit(c.column_name) || ', :NEW.' || q(c.column_name) || ');');
                                ap('    END IF;');
                            ELSE
                                ap('    IF NOT INSERTING THEN');
                                ap('        v_old_row.put(' || lit(c.column_name) || ', ' ||
                                   to_char_expr(':OLD.' || q(c.column_name), c.data_type) || ');');
                                ap('    END IF;');
                                ap('    IF NOT DELETING THEN');
                                ap('        v_new_row.put(' || lit(c.column_name) || ', ' ||
                                   to_char_expr(':NEW.' || q(c.column_name), c.data_type) || ');');
                                ap('    END IF;');
                            END IF;

                            IF NOT v_track THEN
                                ap('');
                                CONTINUE;
                            END IF;
                            v_has_cols := TRUE;

                            -- A NULL inserted or deleted is not a change, so it gets no row
                            -- (the snapshot still has the column)
                            ap('    IF (INSERTING AND :NEW.' || q(c.column_name) || ' IS NOT NULL)' ||
                               ' OR (DELETING AND :OLD.' || q(c.column_name) || ' IS NOT NULL)' ||
                               ' OR (UPDATING AND ' || changed_predicate(c.column_name, c.data_type) || ') THEN');
                            ap('        l_has_changes := TRUE;');
                            ap('        v_col_obj := JSON_OBJECT_T();');
                            ap('        v_col_obj.put(''column_name'', ' || lit(c.column_name) || ');');
                            ap('        v_col_obj.put(''data_type'', ' || lit(UPPER(c.data_type)) || ');');
                            ap('        v_col_obj.put(''old_value'', CASE WHEN INSERTING THEN NULL ELSE ' ||
                               to_char_expr(':OLD.' || q(c.column_name), c.data_type) || ' END);');
                            ap('        v_col_obj.put(''new_value'', CASE WHEN DELETING THEN NULL ELSE ' ||
                               to_char_expr(':NEW.' || q(c.column_name), c.data_type) || ' END);');
                            ap('        v_cols_arr.append(v_col_obj);');
                            ap('    END IF;');
                            ap('');
                        END LOOP;

                        -- An INSERT or DELETE is always recorded, even with no non-NULL column
                        ap('    IF UPDATING AND NOT l_has_changes THEN');
                        ap('        RETURN;');
                        ap('    END IF;');
                        ap('');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''old_row'', v_old_row);');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''new_row'', v_new_row);');
                        ap('    v_audit_json.put(''columns'', v_cols_arr);');
                        ap('');
                        ap('    -- Write audit');
                        ap('    util_audit.capture_audit(v_audit_json);');
                        ap('');
                        ap('EXCEPTION');
                        ap('    WHEN OTHERS THEN');
                        ap('        -- Do not break business DML; record the failure instead');
                        ap('        l_err_code  := SQLCODE;');
                        ap('        l_err_msg   := SUBSTRB(SQLERRM, 1, 4000);');
                        ap('        l_err_trace := SUBSTRB(DBMS_UTILITY.FORMAT_ERROR_BACKTRACE, 1, 4000);');
                        ap('        BEGIN');
                        ap('            util_audit.log_error(' || v_table_lit || ', l_action, l_pk,');
                        ap('                l_err_code, l_err_msg, l_err_trace);');
                        ap('        EXCEPTION');
                        ap('            WHEN OTHERS THEN');
                        ap('                log_direct;');
                        ap('        END;');
                        ap('END;');

                        IF NOT v_has_cols THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20003, 'No auditable columns found for table: ' || v_table_name);
                        END IF;

                        RETURN v_sql;
                    END get_trigger_ddl;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Create trigger
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE create_audit_trigger(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_action     IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'EXECUTE'
                    ) IS
                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128) := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_trg_name   VARCHAR2(128) := trig_name(p_table_name);
                        v_sql        CLOB          := get_trigger_ddl(p_table_name);
                        v_error      VARCHAR2(4000);
                    BEGIN
                        IF norm_name(p_action) = 'GENERATE' THEN
                            exec_sql(v_sql, p_action);
                            report_child_tables(v_table_name);
                            RETURN;
                        END IF;

                        -- Register first: the trigger DDL commits, which also saves this row.
                        -- An existing flag is kept, so regenerating a trigger (e.g. after
                        -- ALTER TABLE) does not re-enable a disabled table.
                        MERGE INTO util_audit_config c
                        USING (SELECT v_table_name table_name FROM dual) src
                        ON (c.table_name = src.table_name)
                        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
                            INSERT (table_name, enabled_flag, created_on, created_by)
                            VALUES (src.table_name, 'Y', SYSDATE, USER);

                        -- Create it disabled and enable it only when it compiled: an invalid
                        -- enabled trigger would block every change to the table
                        v_sql := REPLACE(v_sql, 'FOR EACH ROW' || CHR(10), 'FOR EACH ROW' || CHR(10) || 'DISABLE' || CHR(10));
                        BEGIN
                            exec_sql(v_sql, p_action);
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                IF SQLCODE <> -24344 THEN  -- created with compilation errors
                                    RAISE;
                                END IF;
                        END;
                        SELECT MIN(text) INTO v_error
                        FROM user_errors
                        WHERE name = v_trg_name AND type = 'TRIGGER' AND attribute = 'ERROR';
                        IF v_error IS NOT NULL THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20006, 'The audit trigger for ' || v_table_name ||
                                ' did not compile, so it was left disabled: ' || v_error);
                        END IF;
                        exec_sql('ALTER TRIGGER ' || q(v_trg_name) || ' ENABLE', p_action);

                        -- Then remove any other trigger on the table that calls util_audit
                        -- (an older name, or a util_audit v1 AIUD_<table>_AUD trigger), so
                        -- rows are not audited twice. Creating first leaves no gap.
                        FOR t IN (
                            SELECT trigger_name
                            FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name
                              AND trigger_name <> v_trg_name
                        ) LOOP
                            exec_sql('DROP TRIGGER ' || q(t.trigger_name), p_action);
                        END LOOP;

                        report_child_tables(v_table_name);
                    END create_audit_trigger;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Per-table excluded columns
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- The list, upper case, checked against the table: a misspelt name
                    -- would leave the real column audited without anyone noticing
                    FUNCTION checked_columns(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2, p_columns IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        v_columns VARCHAR2(4000) := UPPER(REPLACE(TRIM(BOTH ',' FROM REPLACE(p_columns, ' ')), ',,', ','));
                        v_col     VARCHAR2(4000);
                        v_cnt     NUMBER;
                        i         PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                    BEGIN
                        LOOP
                            v_col := REGEXP_SUBSTR(v_columns, '[^,]+', 1, i);
                            EXIT WHEN v_col IS NULL;
                            SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_cnt FROM user_tab_columns
                             WHERE table_name = p_table_name AND column_name = v_col;
                            IF v_cnt = 0 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20007, p_table_name || ' has no column ' || v_col || '.');
                            END IF;
                            i := i + 1;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN v_columns;
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE scrub_columns(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns    IN VARCHAR2
                    ) IS
                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128)  := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_columns    VARCHAR2(4000) := checked_columns(v_table_name, p_columns);
                        v_col        VARCHAR2(4000);
                        v_patch      VARCHAR2(4000);
                        v_events     NUMBER;
                        i            PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                    BEGIN
                        LOOP
                            v_col := REGEXP_SUBSTR(v_columns, '[^,]+', 1, i);
                            EXIT WHEN v_col IS NULL;
                            -- {"COL":null}: JSON_MERGEPATCH removes the key
                            SELECT JSON_OBJECT(KEY v_col VALUE NULL NULL ON NULL) INTO v_patch FROM dual;
                            UPDATE util_audit_txn
                               SET old_row_json = JSON_MERGEPATCH(old_row_json, v_patch RETURNING CLOB),
                                   new_row_json = JSON_MERGEPATCH(new_row_json, v_patch RETURNING CLOB)
                             WHERE table_name = v_table_name
                               AND (old_row_json IS NOT NULL OR new_row_json IS NOT NULL);
                            v_events := SQL%ROWCOUNT;
                            DELETE FROM util_audit_records
                             WHERE table_name = v_table_name AND column_name = v_col;
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Removed ' || v_col || ' from ' || v_events || ' snapshot(s) and ' ||
                                                 SQL%ROWCOUNT || ' column change(s) of ' || v_table_name || '.');
                            i := i + 1;
                        END LOOP;
                    END scrub_columns;

                    PROCEDURE set_table_excluded_columns(
                        p_table_name    IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns       IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_regenerate    IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
                        p_scrub_history IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
                    ) IS
                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128)  := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_columns    VARCHAR2(4000) := checked_columns(v_table_name, p_columns);
                        v_has_trg    NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        -- The key identifies the row in every event; it has to be recorded
                        FOR k IN (
                            SELECT cols.column_name
                            FROM user_constraints cons
                            JOIN user_cons_columns cols ON cols.constraint_name = cons.constraint_name
                            WHERE cons.table_name = v_table_name AND cons.constraint_type = 'P'
                        ) LOOP
                            IF in_list(v_columns, k.column_name) THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20008, k.column_name || ' is part of the primary key of ' ||
                                    v_table_name || ' and cannot be excluded.');
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        MERGE INTO util_audit_config c
                        USING (SELECT v_table_name table_name FROM dual) src
                        ON (c.table_name = src.table_name)
                        WHEN MATCHED THEN
                            UPDATE SET excluded_columns = v_columns
                        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
                            INSERT (table_name, enabled_flag, created_on, created_by, excluded_columns)
                            VALUES (src.table_name, 'Y', SYSDATE, USER, v_columns);

                        IF p_regenerate THEN
                            SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_has_trg
                            FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name;
                            IF v_has_trg > 0 THEN
                                create_audit_trigger(v_table_name);
                            END IF;
                        END IF;

                        IF p_scrub_history AND v_columns IS NOT NULL THEN
                            scrub_columns(v_table_name, v_columns);
                        END IF;
                    END set_table_excluded_columns;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Per-table ignored columns
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE set_table_ignored_columns(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns    IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_regenerate IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE
                    ) IS
                        v_table_name VARCHAR2(128)  := norm_name(p_table_name);
                        v_columns    VARCHAR2(4000) := UPPER(REPLACE(TRIM(BOTH ',' FROM REPLACE(p_columns, ' ')), ',,', ','));
                        v_has_trg    NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        MERGE INTO util_audit_config c
                        USING (SELECT v_table_name table_name FROM dual) src
                        ON (c.table_name = src.table_name)
                        WHEN MATCHED THEN
                            UPDATE SET ignored_columns = v_columns
                        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
                            INSERT (table_name, enabled_flag, created_on, created_by, ignored_columns)
                            VALUES (src.table_name, 'Y', SYSDATE, USER, v_columns);

                        IF p_regenerate THEN
                            SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_has_trg
                            FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                            WHERE table_name = v_table_name;
                            IF v_has_trg > 0 THEN
                                create_audit_trigger(v_table_name);
                            END IF;
                        END IF;
                    END set_table_ignored_columns;

                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Public: Re-create all triggers
                    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE recreate_all_triggers IS
                        v_failed PLS_INTEGER := 0;
                    BEGIN
                        FOR t IN (
                            SELECT DISTINCT table_name
                            FROM v_util_audit_triggers
                            WHERE table_name IN (SELECT table_name FROM util_audit_config)
                            ORDER BY table_name
                        ) LOOP
                            BEGIN
                                create_audit_trigger(t.table_name);
                                DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Re-created trigger for ' || t.table_name);
                            EXCEPTION
                                WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                    v_failed := v_failed + 1;
                                    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('FAILED for ' || t.table_name || ': ' || SQLERRM);
                            END;
                        END LOOP;

                        IF v_failed > 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20004, v_failed || ' trigger(s) could not be re-created. See the output for details.');
                        END IF;
                    END recreate_all_triggers;

                END util_audit_gen;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-query-spec (
        execution {
            sequence: 90
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package util_audit_query (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE util_audit_query AS
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- util_audit_query
                    --
                    -- Builds the query for an "audit history" region in another APEX app: the
                    -- changes recorded for the row a page is showing, found by that page's
                    -- primary key items.
                    --
                    --   p_table_name     audited table the page edits
                    --   p_key_items      page items holding the primary key, comma-separated,
                    --                    in key column order. Default: P<p_page_id>_<column>.
                    --   p_page_id        page number in the other app (used for the default)
                    --   p_style          COLUMNS: one row per changed column, old and new value
                    --                    EVENTS:  one row per change, listing changed columns
                    --   p_columns        only show these columns (comma-separated). Null = all
                    --   p_child_tables   also show changes to rows of these audited child
                    --                    tables that point at this row (comma-separated)
                    --   p_schema         schema that owns util_audit, when the other app parses
                    --                    as a different schema. Null = same schema
                    --   p_friendly_names Y: "Hire Date" instead of HIRE_DATE
                    --
                    -- Result columns: CHANGED_AT, CHANGED_BY, ACTION, [TABLE_NAME, RECORD_KEY
                    -- when child tables are included], then FIELD, OLD_VALUE, NEW_VALUE
                    -- (COLUMNS) or FIELDS_CHANGED (EVENTS). Newest first.
                    --
                    -- util_audit_apx writes the same region as APEXlang source.
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                    FUNCTION get_history_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                    -- The page items the region must submit, comma-separated
                    FUNCTION get_key_items(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id    IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL
                    ) RETURN VARCHAR2;

                    -- The same query keyed on one bind, :SAMPLE_KEY, holding a PK_VALUE_VC
                    -- value. Used to preview the result for an existing row.
                    FUNCTION get_preview_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                    -- One row of history(). A package type, so installing needs no
                    -- CREATE TYPE privilege.
                    TYPE t_history_row IS RECORD (
                        changed_at     TIMESTAMP(6),
                        changed_by     VARCHAR2(255),
                        action         VARCHAR2(6),
                        table_name     VARCHAR2(255),
                        record_key     VARCHAR2(4000),
                        field          VARCHAR2(255),
                        old_value      VARCHAR2(4000),
                        new_value      VARCHAR2(4000),
                        fields_changed VARCHAR2(4000),
                        transaction_id VARCHAR2(64)
                    );
                    TYPE t_history_tab IS TABLE OF t_history_row;

                    -- The history as rows, for any region type:
                    --   select * from table(util_audit_query.history('EMP', :P10_EMP_ID))
                    -- p_key1 .. p_key4 are the key column values, in key column order.
                    -- COLUMNS fills FIELD, OLD_VALUE, NEW_VALUE; EVENTS fills FIELDS_CHANGED.
                    -- TABLE_NAME and RECORD_KEY tell rows of child tables apart.
                    FUNCTION history(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key1           IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key2           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_key3           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_key4           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_max_rows       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL
                    ) RETURN t_history_tab PIPELINED;

                    -- SQL for a region that reads history(): short, and follows util_audit
                    -- upgrades without being regenerated
                    FUNCTION get_history_function_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                END util_audit_query;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-query-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 100
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit_query (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit_query AS

                    TYPE t_names IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(128) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;
                    TYPE t_exprs IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(4000) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;

                    c_name_pattern CONSTANT VARCHAR2(40) := '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_$#]*$';

                    FUNCTION lit(p_text IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN '''' || REPLACE(p_text, '''', '''''') || '''';
                    END;

                    -- JSON path for a column of a row snapshot, quoted so any name works
                    FUNCTION jpath(p_column IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN lit('$."' || p_column || '"');
                    END;

                    -- Comma- or colon-separated list, trimmed, empty entries dropped.
                    -- Line breaks and other control characters separate entries too.
                    FUNCTION split(p_list IN VARCHAR2, p_upper IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE) RETURN t_names IS
                        l_out  t_names;
                        l_item VARCHAR2(4000);
                        i      PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                    BEGIN
                        LOOP
                            l_item := REGEXP_SUBSTR(p_list, '[^,:[:cntrl:]]+', 1, i);
                            EXIT WHEN l_item IS NULL;
                            l_item := TRIM(l_item);
                            IF l_item IS NOT NULL THEN
                                l_out(l_out.COUNT + 1) := CASE WHEN p_upper THEN UPPER(l_item) ELSE l_item END;
                            END IF;
                            i := i + 1;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l_out;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION in_names(p_names IN t_names) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_out VARCHAR2(32767);
                    BEGIN
                        FOR i IN 1 .. p_names.COUNT LOOP
                            l_out := l_out || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ', ' END || lit(p_names(i));
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN '(' || l_out || ')';
                    END;

                    FUNCTION pk_columns(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN t_names IS
                        l_cols t_names;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT cols.column_name
                        BULK COLLECT INTO l_cols
                        FROM user_constraints cons
                        JOIN user_cons_columns cols
                          ON cols.constraint_name = cons.constraint_name
                        WHERE cons.table_name = p_table_name
                          AND cons.constraint_type = 'P'
                        ORDER BY cols.position;

                        IF l_cols.COUNT = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20020, p_table_name || ' has no primary key.');
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_cols;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION norm_table(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_table_name));
                        l_cnt   NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO l_cnt FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = l_table;
                        IF l_cnt = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20023, 'Table not found in schema: ' || l_table);
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_table;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION resolve_items(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items  IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_page_id    IN NUMBER
                    ) RETURN t_names IS
                        l_pk    t_names := pk_columns(p_table_name);
                        l_items t_names;
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_key_items IS NOT NULL THEN
                            l_items := split(p_key_items);
                            IF l_items.COUNT <> l_pk.COUNT THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20021, p_table_name || ' has ' || l_pk.COUNT ||
                                    ' key column(s), so give ' || l_pk.COUNT || ' page item(s), in this order: ' ||
                                    REPLACE(in_names(l_pk), '''', ''));
                            END IF;
                        ELSIF p_page_id IS NULL THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20022, 'Give the page number, or the page items that hold the key.');
                        ELSE
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk.COUNT LOOP
                                l_items(i) := 'P' || p_page_id || '_' || l_pk(i);
                            END LOOP;
                        END IF;

                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_items.COUNT LOOP
                            IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(l_items(i), c_name_pattern) THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20024, 'Not a valid page item name: ' || l_items(i));
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l_items;
                    END;

                    -- The expression that equals PK_VALUE_VC for the row: the single key
                    -- value, or the key object the trigger writes for a composite key
                    FUNCTION key_expr(p_pk IN t_names, p_exprs IN t_exprs) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_out VARCHAR2(32767);
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_pk.COUNT = 1 THEN
                            RETURN p_exprs(1);
                        END IF;
                        FOR i IN 1 .. p_pk.COUNT LOOP
                            l_out := l_out || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ', ' END || lit(p_pk(i)) || ' value ' || p_exprs(i);
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN 'json_object(' || l_out || ')';
                    END;

                    FUNCTION build(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_exprs          IN t_exprs,
                        p_header         IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_full_shape     IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_table    VARCHAR2(128) := norm_table(p_table_name);
                        l_style    VARCHAR2(10)  := NVL(UPPER(p_style), 'COLUMNS');
                        l_pk       t_names       := pk_columns(l_table);
                        l_cols     t_names       := split(p_columns);
                        l_children t_names       := split(p_child_tables);
                        l_pfx      VARCHAR2(200);
                        a          VARCHAR2(1);
                        l_field    VARCHAR2(200);
                        l_where    CLOB;
                        l_notes    VARCHAR2(4000);
                        l_sql      CLOB;
                        l_cnt      NUMBER;
                        l_fk_conds VARCHAR2(32767);

                        FUNCTION field_of(p_alias IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        BEGIN
                            RETURN CASE WHEN NVL(p_friendly_names, 'Y') = 'Y'
                                        THEN 'initcap(replace(' || p_alias || '.column_name, ''_'', '' ''))'
                                        ELSE p_alias || '.column_name' END;
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        IF l_style NOT IN ('COLUMNS', 'EVENTS') THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20025, 'Style must be COLUMNS or EVENTS.');
                        END IF;
                        IF p_schema IS NOT NULL THEN
                            IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(TRIM(p_schema), c_name_pattern) THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20026, 'Not a valid schema name: ' || p_schema);
                            END IF;
                            l_pfx := UPPER(TRIM(p_schema)) || '.';
                        END IF;
                        a := CASE l_style WHEN 'COLUMNS' THEN 'h' ELSE 'e' END;
                        l_field := field_of('r');

                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_cols.COUNT LOOP
                            SELECT COUNT(*) INTO l_cnt FROM user_tab_columns
                            WHERE table_name = l_table AND column_name = l_cols(i);
                            IF l_cnt = 0 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20027, l_table || ' has no column ' || l_cols(i) || '.');
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        -- This row
                        l_where := '(' || a || '.table_name = ' || lit(l_table) ||
                                   ' and ' || a || '.pk_value_vc = ' || key_expr(l_pk, p_exprs);
                        IF l_cols.COUNT > 0 THEN
                            IF l_style = 'COLUMNS' THEN
                                l_where := l_where || CHR(10) || '          and h.column_name in ' || in_names(l_cols);
                            ELSE
                                l_where := l_where || CHR(10) || '          and exists (select 1 from ' || l_pfx ||
                                           'util_audit_records r where r.transaction_id = e.transaction_id and r.column_name in ' ||
                                           in_names(l_cols) || ')';
                            END IF;
                        END IF;
                        l_where := l_where || ')';

                        -- Child rows: their row snapshot holds a foreign key value equal to
                        -- this row's key, before or after the change
                        FOR c IN 1 .. l_children.COUNT LOOP
                            l_fk_conds := NULL;
                            FOR fk IN (
                                SELECT constraint_name
                                FROM v_util_audit_child_tables
                                WHERE parent_table = l_table
                                  AND child_table  = l_children(c)
                                ORDER BY constraint_name
                            ) LOOP
                                DECLARE
                                    l_old  VARCHAR2(4000);
                                    l_new  VARCHAR2(4000);
                                    l_idx  PLS_INTEGER;
                                    l_skip BOOLEAN := FALSE;
                                BEGIN
                                    FOR p IN (
                                        SELECT cc.column_name child_col, pc.column_name parent_col
                                        FROM user_constraints uc
                                        JOIN user_cons_columns cc ON cc.constraint_name = uc.constraint_name
                                        JOIN user_cons_columns pc ON pc.constraint_name = uc.r_constraint_name
                                                                 AND pc.position = cc.position
                                        WHERE uc.constraint_name = fk.constraint_name
                                        ORDER BY cc.position
                                    ) LOOP
                                        l_idx := NULL;
                                        FOR k IN 1 .. l_pk.COUNT LOOP
                                            IF l_pk(k) = p.parent_col THEN l_idx := k; END IF;
                                        END LOOP;
                                        IF l_idx IS NULL THEN
                                            l_skip := TRUE;
                                            EXIT;
                                        END IF;
                                        l_old := l_old || CASE WHEN l_old IS NOT NULL THEN ' and ' END ||
                                                 'json_value(' || a || '.old_row_json, ' || jpath(p.child_col) || ') = ' || p_exprs(l_idx);
                                        l_new := l_new || CASE WHEN l_new IS NOT NULL THEN ' and ' END ||
                                                 'json_value(' || a || '.new_row_json, ' || jpath(p.child_col) || ') = ' || p_exprs(l_idx);
                                    END LOOP;
                                    IF l_skip THEN
                                        l_notes := l_notes || '-- ' || l_children(c) || ' (' || fk.constraint_name ||
                                                   ') skipped: it references a unique key, not the primary key' || CHR(10);
                                    ELSE
                                        l_fk_conds := l_fk_conds || CASE WHEN l_fk_conds IS NOT NULL THEN CHR(10) || '             or ' END ||
                                                      '(' || l_old || ')' || CHR(10) || '             or (' || l_new || ')';
                                    END IF;
                                END;
                            END LOOP;

                            IF l_fk_conds IS NULL THEN
                                IF l_notes IS NULL OR INSTR(l_notes, '-- ' || l_children(c) || ' (') = 0 THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20028, l_children(c) || ' does not reference ' || l_table || '.');
                                END IF;
                            ELSE
                                l_where := l_where || CHR(10) || '    or (' || a || '.table_name = ' || lit(l_children(c)) ||
                                           CHR(10) || '        and (' || l_fk_conds || '))';
                            END IF;
                        END LOOP;

                        l_sql := p_header || l_notes;
                        IF l_style = 'COLUMNS' THEN
                            l_sql := l_sql ||
                                'select h.audit_ts as changed_at,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       h.username as changed_by,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       h.transaction_type as action,' || CHR(10) ||
                                CASE WHEN l_children.COUNT > 0 OR p_full_shape THEN
                                '       h.table_name as table_name,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       h.pk_value_vc as record_key,' || CHR(10) END ||
                                '       ' || field_of('h') || ' as field,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       coalesce(h.old_value, dbms_lob.substr(h.old_clob, 1000, 1)) as old_value,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       coalesce(h.new_value, dbms_lob.substr(h.new_clob, 1000, 1)) as new_value' ||
                                CASE WHEN p_full_shape THEN ',' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       cast(null as varchar2(4000)) as fields_changed,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       h.transaction_id as transaction_id' END || CHR(10) ||
                                '  from ' || l_pfx || 'v_util_audit_row_history h' || CHR(10) ||
                                ' where ' || l_where || CHR(10) ||
                                ' order by h.audit_ts desc, h.transaction_id, h.column_name';
                        ELSE
                            l_sql := l_sql ||
                                'select e.audit_ts as changed_at,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       e.username as changed_by,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       e.transaction_type as action,' || CHR(10) ||
                                CASE WHEN l_children.COUNT > 0 OR p_full_shape THEN
                                '       e.table_name as table_name,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       e.pk_value_vc as record_key,' || CHR(10) END ||
                                CASE WHEN p_full_shape THEN
                                '       cast(null as varchar2(255)) as field,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       cast(null as varchar2(4000)) as old_value,' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       cast(null as varchar2(4000)) as new_value,' || CHR(10) END ||
                                '       (select listagg(' || l_field || ', '', '' on overflow truncate ''...'' with count)' || CHR(10) ||
                                '                 within group (order by r.column_name)' || CHR(10) ||
                                '          from ' || l_pfx || 'util_audit_records r' || CHR(10) ||
                                '         where r.transaction_id = e.transaction_id) as fields_changed' ||
                                CASE WHEN p_full_shape THEN ',' || CHR(10) ||
                                '       e.transaction_id as transaction_id' END || CHR(10) ||
                                '  from ' || l_pfx || 'v_util_audit_events e' || CHR(10) ||
                                ' where ' || l_where || CHR(10) ||
                                ' order by e.audit_ts desc, e.transaction_id';
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_sql;
                    END build;

                    FUNCTION get_key_items(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id    IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL
                    ) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_items t_names := resolve_items(norm_table(p_table_name), p_key_items, p_page_id);
                        l_out   VARCHAR2(4000);
                    BEGIN
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_items.COUNT LOOP
                            l_out := l_out || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ',' END || l_items(i);
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l_out;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION get_history_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128) := norm_table(p_table_name);
                        l_items t_names       := resolve_items(l_table, p_key_items, p_page_id);
                        l_exprs t_exprs;
                    BEGIN
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_items.COUNT LOOP
                            l_exprs(i) := ':' || l_items(i);
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN build(l_table, l_exprs,
                                     '-- Audit history for ' || l_table || ' (generated by util_audit_query)' || CHR(10) ||
                                     '-- Page Items to Submit: ' || get_key_items(l_table, p_key_items, p_page_id) || CHR(10),
                                     p_style, p_columns, p_child_tables, p_schema, p_friendly_names);
                    END;

                    FUNCTION get_preview_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128) := norm_table(p_table_name);
                        l_pk    t_names       := pk_columns(l_table);
                        l_exprs t_exprs;
                    BEGIN
                        -- :SAMPLE_KEY is a PK_VALUE_VC value; a composite one is a JSON object
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk.COUNT LOOP
                            l_exprs(i) := CASE WHEN l_pk.COUNT = 1 THEN ':SAMPLE_KEY'
                                               ELSE 'json_value(:SAMPLE_KEY, ' || jpath(l_pk(i)) || ')' END;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN build(l_table, l_exprs, NULL, p_style, p_columns, p_child_tables, NULL, p_friendly_names);
                    END;

                    FUNCTION history(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key1           IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key2           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_key3           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_key4           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_max_rows       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL
                    ) RETURN t_history_tab PIPELINED IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128);
                        l_pk    t_names;
                        l_exprs t_exprs;
                        l_keys  t_exprs;
                        l_key   VARCHAR2(4000);
                        l_obj   json_object_t;
                        l_cur   INTEGER;
                        l_rc    SYS_REFCURSOR;
                        l_count PLS_INTEGER := 0;
                        l_recs  t_history_tab;
                        l_sql   CLOB;
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_key1 IS NULL THEN
                            RETURN;
                        END IF;
                        l_table := norm_table(p_table_name);
                        l_pk    := pk_columns(l_table);
                        l_keys(1) := p_key1; l_keys(2) := p_key2; l_keys(3) := p_key3; l_keys(4) := p_key4;
                        IF l_pk.COUNT > 4 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20030, l_table || ' has more than 4 key columns.');
                        END IF;

                        -- The key exactly as the trigger stores it in PK_VALUE_VC
                        IF l_pk.COUNT = 1 THEN
                            l_key := p_key1;
                        ELSE
                            l_obj := json_object_t();
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk.COUNT LOOP
                                l_obj.put(l_pk(i), l_keys(i));
                            END LOOP;
                            l_key := l_obj.to_string;
                        END IF;

                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_pk.COUNT LOOP
                            l_exprs(i) := CASE WHEN l_pk.COUNT = 1 THEN ':SAMPLE_KEY'
                                               ELSE 'json_value(:SAMPLE_KEY, ' || jpath(l_pk(i)) || ')' END;
                        END LOOP;

                        l_sql := build(l_table, l_exprs, NULL, p_style, p_columns, p_child_tables,
                                       NULL, p_friendly_names, p_full_shape => TRUE);
                        l_cur := DBMS_SQL.OPEN_CURSOR;
                        DBMS_SQL.PARSE(l_cur, l_sql, DBMS_SQL.NATIVE);
                        DBMS_SQL.BIND_VARIABLE(l_cur, 'SAMPLE_KEY', l_key);
                        l_count := DBMS_SQL.EXECUTE(l_cur);
                        l_rc := DBMS_SQL.TO_REFCURSOR(l_cur);
                        l_cur := NULL;
                        l_count := 0;
                        LOOP
                            FETCH l_rc BULK COLLECT INTO l_recs LIMIT 200;
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_recs.COUNT LOOP
                                EXIT WHEN p_max_rows IS NOT NULL AND l_count >= p_max_rows;
                                l_count := l_count + 1;
                                PIPE ROW (l_recs(i));
                            END LOOP;
                            EXIT WHEN l_recs.COUNT < 200 OR (p_max_rows IS NOT NULL AND l_count >= p_max_rows);
                        END LOOP;
                        CLOSE l_rc;
                        RETURN;
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            -- Includes NO_DATA_NEEDED, when the caller stops fetching early
                            IF l_rc%ISOPEN THEN
                                CLOSE l_rc;
                            END IF;
                            IF l_cur IS NOT NULL AND DBMS_SQL.IS_OPEN(l_cur) THEN
                                DBMS_SQL.CLOSE_CURSOR(l_cur);
                            END IF;
                            RAISE;
                    END history;

                    FUNCTION get_history_function_query(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y'
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128) := norm_table(p_table_name);
                        l_items t_names       := resolve_items(l_table, p_key_items, p_page_id);
                        l_style VARCHAR2(10)  := NVL(UPPER(p_style), 'COLUMNS');
                        l_cols  t_names       := split(p_columns);
                        l_kids  t_names       := split(p_child_tables);
                        l_list  VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_sql   VARCHAR2(32767);
                    BEGIN
                        IF l_items.COUNT > 4 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20030, l_table || ' has more than 4 key columns.');
                        END IF;
                        -- Checks style, columns, child tables and schema; the query is not used
                        l_sql := get_history_query(p_table_name, p_key_items, p_page_id, p_style,
                                                   p_columns, p_child_tables, p_schema, p_friendly_names);

                        l_sql := '-- Audit history for ' || l_table || ' (generated by util_audit_query)' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '-- Page Items to Submit: ' || get_key_items(l_table, p_key_items, p_page_id) || CHR(10) ||
                                 'select changed_at,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '       changed_by,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '       action,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 CASE WHEN l_kids.COUNT > 0 THEN
                                 '       table_name,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '       record_key,' || CHR(10) END ||
                                 CASE WHEN l_style = 'COLUMNS' THEN
                                 '       field,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '       old_value,' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '       new_value' || CHR(10)
                                 ELSE
                                 '       fields_changed' || CHR(10) END ||
                                 '  from table(' ||
                                 CASE WHEN p_schema IS NOT NULL THEN UPPER(TRIM(p_schema)) || '.' END ||
                                 'util_audit_query.history(' || CHR(10) ||
                                 '           p_table_name => ' || lit(l_table);
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_items.COUNT LOOP
                            l_sql := l_sql || ',' || CHR(10) || '           p_key' || i || '       => :' || l_items(i);
                        END LOOP;
                        IF l_style <> 'COLUMNS' THEN
                            l_sql := l_sql || ',' || CHR(10) || '           p_style      => ''EVENTS''';
                        END IF;
                        IF l_cols.COUNT > 0 THEN
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_cols.COUNT LOOP
                                l_list := l_list || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ',' END || l_cols(i);
                            END LOOP;
                            l_sql := l_sql || ',' || CHR(10) || '           p_columns    => ' || lit(l_list);
                            l_list := NULL;
                        END IF;
                        IF l_kids.COUNT > 0 THEN
                            FOR i IN 1 .. l_kids.COUNT LOOP
                                l_list := l_list || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ',' END || l_kids(i);
                            END LOOP;
                            l_sql := l_sql || ',' || CHR(10) || '           p_child_tables => ' || lit(l_list);
                        END IF;
                        IF NVL(p_friendly_names, 'Y') <> 'Y' THEN
                            l_sql := l_sql || ',' || CHR(10) || '           p_friendly_names => ''N''';
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_sql || '))';
                    END get_history_function_query;

                END util_audit_query;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-apx-spec (
        execution {
            sequence: 110
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package util_audit_apx (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE util_audit_apx AS
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- util_audit_apx
                    --
                    -- Writes an "audit history" region as APEXlang (.apx) source, ready to
                    -- paste into a page file of another app. The parameters are the same as
                    -- util_audit_query.get_history_query, plus where the region goes:
                    --
                    --   p_region_id      static id: lower-case letters, digits and dashes
                    --   p_sequence       sequence within the slot
                    --   p_slot           page slot, e.g. body
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                    -- An APEXlang region of the Audit History plugin type (the plugin ships
                    -- with the Util Audit app: shared-components/plugins/region/utilAuditHistory)
                    FUNCTION get_plugin_region_apx(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_region_id      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'audit-history',
                        p_sequence       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 100,
                        p_slot           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'body'
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                    -- A complete APEXlang classic report region for a page's .apx file
                    FUNCTION get_history_region_apx(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_region_id      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'audit-history',
                        p_sequence       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 100,
                        p_slot           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'body'
                    ) RETURN CLOB;

                END util_audit_apx;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-apx-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 120
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit_apx (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit_apx AS

                    TYPE t_names IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(128) INDEX BY PLS_INTEGER;

                    -- Comma-separated list, trimmed, upper case, empty entries dropped
                    FUNCTION split(p_list IN VARCHAR2) RETURN t_names IS
                        l_out  t_names;
                        l_item VARCHAR2(4000);
                        i      PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                    BEGIN
                        LOOP
                            l_item := REGEXP_SUBSTR(p_list, '[^,:[:cntrl:]]+', 1, i);
                            EXIT WHEN l_item IS NULL;
                            l_item := TRIM(l_item);
                            IF l_item IS NOT NULL THEN
                                l_out(l_out.COUNT + 1) := UPPER(l_item);
                            END IF;
                            i := i + 1;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l_out;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION joined(p_names IN t_names) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l VARCHAR2(32767);
                    BEGIN
                        FOR i IN 1 .. p_names.COUNT LOOP
                            l := l || CASE WHEN i > 1 THEN ',' END || p_names(i);
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN l;
                    END;

                    -- Every value that ends up in the .apx text is checked, so the output
                    -- cannot break out of its property
                    PROCEDURE check_region(p_region_id IN VARCHAR2, p_sequence IN NUMBER, p_slot IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(p_region_id, '^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$') THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20029, 'Region id must be lower-case letters, digits and dashes.');
                        END IF;
                        IF p_sequence IS NULL OR p_sequence < 0 OR p_sequence <> TRUNC(p_sequence) THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20031, 'Sequence must be a whole number, 0 or more.');
                        END IF;
                        IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(p_slot, '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$') THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20032, 'Not a valid slot name: ' || p_slot);
                        END IF;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION get_plugin_region_apx(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_region_id      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'audit-history',
                        p_sequence       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 100,
                        p_slot           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'body'
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_table VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_table_name));
                        l_items t_names       := split(util_audit_query.get_key_items(p_table_name, p_key_items, p_page_id));
                        l_cols  t_names       := split(p_columns);
                        l_kids  t_names       := split(p_child_tables);
                        l_check CLOB;
                        l_out   CLOB;

                        PROCEDURE ap(p IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        BEGIN
                            l_out := l_out || p || CHR(10);
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        check_region(p_region_id, p_sequence, p_slot);
                        IF l_items.COUNT > 4 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20030, l_table || ' has more than 4 key columns.');
                        END IF;
                        -- Checks columns, child tables and schema; the query itself is not used
                        l_check := util_audit_query.get_history_query(p_table_name, p_key_items, p_page_id, p_style,
                                                     p_columns, p_child_tables, p_schema, p_friendly_names);

                        ap('    region ' || p_region_id || ' (');
                        ap('        name: Audit History');
                        ap('        type: plugin/utilAuditHistory');
                        ap('        settings {');
                        ap('            table: ' || l_table);
                        ap('            keyItems: ' || joined(l_items));
                        ap('            display: ' || CASE WHEN UPPER(p_style) = 'EVENTS' THEN 'events' ELSE 'columns' END);
                        IF l_kids.COUNT > 0 THEN
                            ap('            childTables: ' || joined(l_kids));
                        END IF;
                        IF l_cols.COUNT > 0 THEN
                            ap('            columns: ' || joined(l_cols));
                        END IF;
                        ap('            readableNames: ' || CASE WHEN NVL(p_friendly_names, 'Y') = 'Y' THEN 'true' ELSE 'false' END);
                        ap('            maxRows: 100');
                        ap('            dateFormat: SINCE');
                        IF p_schema IS NOT NULL THEN
                            ap('            utilAuditSchema: ' || UPPER(TRIM(p_schema)));
                        END IF;
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        layout {');
                        ap('            sequence: ' || p_sequence);
                        ap('            slot: ' || p_slot);
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        appearance {');
                        ap('            template: @/standard');
                        ap('            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        messages {');
                        ap('            whenNoDataFound: No changes recorded yet.');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        serverSideCondition {');
                        ap('            type: itemIsNotNull');
                        ap('            item: ' || l_items(1));
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('    )');
                        RETURN l_out;
                    END get_plugin_region_apx;

                    FUNCTION get_history_region_apx(
                        p_table_name     IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_key_items      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_page_id        IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_style          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'COLUMNS',
                        p_columns        IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_child_tables   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_schema         IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
                        p_friendly_names IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'Y',
                        p_region_id      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'audit-history',
                        p_sequence       IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 100,
                        p_slot           IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'body'
                    ) RETURN CLOB IS
                        l_items  t_names       := split(util_audit_query.get_key_items(p_table_name, p_key_items, p_page_id));
                        l_style  VARCHAR2(10)  := NVL(UPPER(p_style), 'COLUMNS');
                        l_query  CLOB := util_audit_query.get_history_function_query(p_table_name, p_key_items, p_page_id, p_style,
                                                                    p_columns, p_child_tables, p_schema, p_friendly_names);
                        l_out    CLOB;
                        l_cols   t_names;
                        l_heads  t_names;
                        l_seq    PLS_INTEGER := 0;
                        l_line   VARCHAR2(32767);
                        l_pos    PLS_INTEGER := 1;
                        l_nl     PLS_INTEGER;

                        -- Three backticks, built so this source never contains them: the app
                        -- embeds this file in a backtick-fenced block of supporting-objects.apx
                        l_fence  CONSTANT VARCHAR2(3) := CHR(96) || CHR(96) || CHR(96);

                        PROCEDURE ap(p IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        BEGIN
                            l_out := l_out || p || CHR(10);
                        END;
                        PROCEDURE col(p_name IN VARCHAR2, p_heading IN VARCHAR2) IS
                        BEGIN
                            l_cols(l_cols.COUNT + 1)   := p_name;
                            l_heads(l_heads.COUNT + 1) := p_heading;
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        check_region(p_region_id, p_sequence, p_slot);

                        col('CHANGED_AT', 'Changed');
                        col('CHANGED_BY', 'By');
                        col('ACTION', 'Action');
                        IF split(p_child_tables).COUNT > 0 THEN
                            col('TABLE_NAME', 'Table');
                            col('RECORD_KEY', 'Record');
                        END IF;
                        IF l_style = 'COLUMNS' THEN
                            col('FIELD', 'Field');
                            col('OLD_VALUE', 'Old Value');
                            col('NEW_VALUE', 'New Value');
                        ELSE
                            col('FIELDS_CHANGED', 'Fields Changed');
                        END IF;

                        ap('    region ' || p_region_id || ' (');
                        ap('        name: Audit History');
                        ap('        type: classicReport');
                        ap('        source {');
                        ap('            location: localDatabase');
                        ap('            type: sqlQuery');
                        ap('            sqlQuery:');
                        ap('                ' || l_fence || 'sql');
                        -- the query, indented, without its leading comment lines
                        l_query := l_query || CHR(10);
                        LOOP
                            l_nl := INSTR(l_query, CHR(10), l_pos);
                            EXIT WHEN l_nl = 0;
                            l_line := SUBSTR(l_query, l_pos, l_nl - l_pos);
                            IF l_line NOT LIKE '-- Audit history%' AND l_line NOT LIKE '-- Page Items%' THEN
                                ap('                ' || l_line);
                            END IF;
                            l_pos := l_nl + 1;
                        END LOOP;
                        ap('                ' || l_fence);
                        ap('            pageItemsToSubmit: [');
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_items.COUNT LOOP
                            ap('                ' || l_items(i));
                        END LOOP;
                        ap('            ]');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        layout {');
                        ap('            sequence: ' || p_sequence);
                        ap('            slot: ' || p_slot);
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        appearance {');
                        ap('            template: @/standard');
                        ap('            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        componentAppearance {');
                        ap('            template: @/standard');
                        ap('            templateOptions: [');
                        ap('                #DEFAULT#');
                        ap('                t-Report--stretch');
                        ap('            ]');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        serverSideCondition {');
                        ap('            type: itemIsNotNull');
                        ap('            item: ' || l_items(1));
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        pagination {');
                        ap('            type: rowRangesXToYOfZWithPagination');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        reportLayout {');
                        ap('            numberOfRowsType: staticValue');
                        ap('            numberOfRows: 25');
                        ap('        }');
                        ap('        messages {');
                        ap('            whenNoDataFound: No changes recorded yet.');
                        ap('        }');
                        FOR i IN 1 .. l_cols.COUNT LOOP
                            l_seq := l_seq + 10;
                            ap('');
                            ap('        column ' || l_cols(i) || ' (');
                            ap('            reportColumnQueryId: ' || i);
                            ap('            derivedColumn: N');
                            ap('            heading {');
                            ap('                heading: ' || l_heads(i));
                            ap('            }');
                            ap('            layout {');
                            ap('                sequence: ' || l_seq);
                            ap('            }');
                            IF l_cols(i) = 'CHANGED_AT' THEN
                                ap('            appearance {');
                                ap('                formatMask: YYYY-MM-DD HH24":"MI');
                                ap('            }');
                            END IF;
                            ap('        )');
                        END LOOP;
                        ap('    )');
                        RETURN l_out;
                    END get_history_region_apx;

                END util_audit_apx;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-archive-spec (
        execution {
            sequence: 130
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package util_audit_archive (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE util_audit_archive AS
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- util_audit_archive_files
                    --
                    -- Moves old audit history out of the database into files, and brings it
                    -- back when needed. One file holds one table's events of one calendar
                    -- month: gzipped JSON lines (.jsonl.gz), one event per line with its
                    -- column changes and row snapshots.
                    --
                    -- Each file goes through these states (UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_FILES.STATUS):
                    --   CREATED   the file is built and held in UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_FILES.CONTENT
                    --   STORED    the file is in its storage and was read back and checked
                    --   PURGED    the month's events were deleted from the audit tables
                    --   RESTORED  the events were loaded back into the audit tables
                    --   FAILED    a step failed; MESSAGE says why. run() tries again.
                    --
                    -- Storage (setting ARCHIVE_STORAGE):
                    --   DATABASE     keep the file in UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_FILES.CONTENT
                    --   AWS4_S3_PKG  S3, through the schema's aws4_s3_pkg (put_object and
                    --                get_object_blob). Settings: ARCHIVE_BUCKET, ARCHIVE_PREFIX
                    --   DBMS_CLOUD   S3 or other object storage through DBMS_CLOUD.
                    --                Settings: ARCHIVE_CREDENTIAL, ARCHIVE_BASE_URI
                    --   CUSTOM       your own code. Settings: ARCHIVE_PUT_PROCEDURE, called as
                    --                proc(p_object_key IN VARCHAR2, p_content IN BLOB), and
                    --                ARCHIVE_GET_FUNCTION, called as
                    --                func(p_object_key IN VARCHAR2) RETURN BLOB
                    --
                    -- Other settings:
                    --   ARCHIVE_KEEP_MONTHS  months kept in the audit tables (default 12)
                    --   ARCHIVE_PURGE        Y: run() deletes archived months from the audit
                    --                        tables. Default N, so the first runs only copy.
                    --
                    -- These procedures commit: each file is its own unit of work.
                    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                    FUNCTION get_setting(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2;

                    PROCEDURE set_setting(p_name IN VARCHAR2, p_value IN VARCHAR2);

                    -- Builds the file for one table and the month that contains p_month.
                    -- Returns the new ARCHIVE_ID, or NULL when the month has no events.
                    FUNCTION archive_month(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_month      IN DATE
                    ) RETURN NUMBER;

                    -- Puts a CREATED file in its storage, reads it back and compares the
                    -- SHA-256. Then STORED; for remote storage the local copy is dropped.
                    PROCEDURE store(p_archive_id IN NUMBER);

                    -- Deletes a STORED file's events from the audit tables, after checking
                    -- the tables still hold exactly the events in the file.
                    PROCEDURE purge(p_archive_id IN NUMBER);

                    -- Loads a file's events back into the audit tables. Events that are
                    -- already there are skipped, so it is safe to repeat.
                    PROCEDURE restore(p_archive_id IN NUMBER);

                    -- The file itself (gzipped JSON lines), from wherever it is kept
                    FUNCTION get_file(p_archive_id IN NUMBER) RETURN BLOB;

                    -- The scheduled work: archive every table's months older than
                    -- ARCHIVE_KEEP_MONTHS, store them, and purge them if ARCHIVE_PURGE = Y.
                    -- Also retries earlier files that did not finish. p_max_files limits
                    -- how many new files one run makes. Prints what it did; raises at the
                    -- end if anything failed, so a scheduler job shows as failed.
                    PROCEDURE run(p_max_files IN PLS_INTEGER DEFAULT 100);

                    -- Creates or replaces the DBMS_SCHEDULER job UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_JOB that
                    -- calls run(). Needs the CREATE JOB privilege.
                    PROCEDURE schedule(p_repeat_interval IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'FREQ=DAILY;BYHOUR=2;BYMINUTE=0');

                    PROCEDURE unschedule;

                END util_audit_archive;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-util-audit-archive-body (
        execution {
            sequence: 140
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Package body util_audit_archive (generated from setup.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                create or replace PACKAGE BODY util_audit_archive AS

                    c_job CONSTANT VARCHAR2(30) := 'UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_JOB';

                    FUNCTION get_setting(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_value util_audit_settings.value%TYPE;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT value INTO l_value FROM util_audit_settings WHERE name = UPPER(p_name);
                        RETURN l_value;
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
                            RETURN NULL;
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE set_setting(p_name IN VARCHAR2, p_value IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        MERGE INTO util_audit_settings s
                        USING (SELECT UPPER(p_name) name FROM dual) n
                        ON (s.name = n.name)
                        WHEN MATCHED THEN
                            UPDATE SET value = p_value, updated_on = SYSDATE,
                                       updated_by = NVL(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), USER)
                        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN
                            INSERT (name, value, updated_on, updated_by)
                            VALUES (n.name, p_value, SYSDATE, NVL(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), USER));
                    END;

                    FUNCTION storage RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN NVL(UPPER(get_setting('ARCHIVE_STORAGE')), 'DATABASE');
                    END;

                    -- A setting that must be there for the chosen storage
                    FUNCTION required(p_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_value VARCHAR2(4000) := get_setting(p_name);
                    BEGIN
                        IF l_value IS NULL THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20040, 'Setting ' || p_name || ' is empty; ' || storage || ' storage needs it.');
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_value;
                    END;

                    -- SHA-256 of the file. DBMS_CRYPTO is not granted to every schema;
                    -- without it the checksum is a SHA-256 chain over 1968-byte blocks,
                    -- marked 'blocks:'. p_like picks the same kind as a stored checksum.
                    FUNCTION sha256(p_blob IN BLOB, p_like IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                        l_hash  RAW(32);
                        l_chunk RAW(1968);
                        l_amt   INTEGER;
                        l_pos   INTEGER := 1;
                        l_len   INTEGER := DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH(p_blob);
                    BEGIN
                        IF p_like IS NULL OR p_like NOT LIKE 'blocks:%' THEN
                            BEGIN
                                EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin :h := dbms_crypto.hash(:b, 4); end;'  -- 4 = HASH_SH256
                                    USING OUT l_hash, p_blob;
                                RETURN LOWER(RAWTOHEX(l_hash));
                            EXCEPTION
                                WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                    IF SQLCODE <> -6550 OR p_like IS NOT NULL THEN  -- -6550: no access to DBMS_CRYPTO
                                        RAISE;
                                    END IF;
                            END;
                        END IF;
                        WHILE l_pos <= l_len LOOP
                            l_amt := 1968;
                            DBMS_LOB.READ(p_blob, l_amt, l_pos, l_chunk);
                            SELECT STANDARD_HASH(l_hash || l_chunk, 'SHA256') INTO l_hash FROM dual;
                            l_pos := l_pos + l_amt;
                        END LOOP;
                        RETURN 'blocks:' || LOWER(RAWTOHEX(l_hash));
                    END;

                    -- Records a problem in its own transaction; p_failed sets FAILED
                    PROCEDURE note(p_archive_id IN NUMBER, p_message IN VARCHAR2, p_failed IN BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE) IS
                        PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;
                        l_failed VARCHAR2(1) := CASE WHEN p_failed THEN 'Y' END;
                    BEGIN
                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files
                           SET status  = CASE WHEN l_failed = 'Y' THEN 'FAILED' ELSE status END,
                               message = SUBSTRB(p_message, 1, 4000)
                         WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        COMMIT;
                    END;

                    -- Where the file goes, e.g. util_audit/HR/table=EMP/month=2025-01/EMP_2025-01_17.jsonl.gz
                    -- (Hive-style folders, so tools such as Athena can query the files)
                    FUNCTION object_key(a IN util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
                    BEGIN
                        RETURN RTRIM(NVL(get_setting('ARCHIVE_PREFIX'), 'util_audit/' || $$PLSQL_UNIT_OWNER), '/') ||
                               '/table=' || a.table_name ||
                               '/month=' || TO_CHAR(a.period_start, 'YYYY-MM', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN') ||
                               '/' || a.file_name;
                    END;

                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Storage adapters. Dynamic SQL, so this package compiles without them.
                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE put_file(p_storage IN VARCHAR2, p_key IN VARCHAR2, p_content IN BLOB, p_location OUT VARCHAR2) IS
                        l_status NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        CASE p_storage
                        WHEN 'AWS4_S3_PKG' THEN
                            -- aws4_s3_pkg does not raise on an HTTP error, so check the status
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'[
                                begin
                                    aws4_s3_pkg.put_object(p_bucket => :b, p_blob => :c, p_object_key => :k,
                                                           p_mimetype => 'application/gzip');
                                    :s := apex_web_service.g_status_code;
                                end;]'
                                USING required('ARCHIVE_BUCKET'), p_content, '/' || p_key, OUT l_status;
                            IF NVL(l_status, 0) <> 200 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20041, 'S3 upload failed with HTTP status ' || NVL(TO_CHAR(l_status), 'none') || '.');
                            END IF;
                            p_location := 's3://' || get_setting('ARCHIVE_BUCKET') || '/' || p_key;
                        WHEN 'DBMS_CLOUD' THEN
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin dbms_cloud.put_object(credential_name => :c, object_uri => :u, contents => :b); end;'
                                USING required('ARCHIVE_CREDENTIAL'), RTRIM(required('ARCHIVE_BASE_URI'), '/') || '/' || p_key, p_content;
                            p_location := RTRIM(get_setting('ARCHIVE_BASE_URI'), '/') || '/' || p_key;
                        WHEN 'CUSTOM' THEN
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin ' || DBMS_ASSERT.QUALIFIED_SQL_NAME(required('ARCHIVE_PUT_PROCEDURE')) ||
                                              '(p_object_key => :k, p_content => :c); end;'
                                USING p_key, p_content;
                            p_location := p_key;
                        WHEN 'DATABASE' THEN
                            p_location := 'UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_FILES.CONTENT';
                        ELSE
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20042, 'Unknown ARCHIVE_STORAGE: ' || p_storage);
                        END CASE;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION fetch_file(a IN util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE) RETURN BLOB IS
                        l_blob BLOB;
                        l_key  VARCHAR2(1000);
                    BEGIN
                        IF a.content IS NOT NULL THEN
                            RETURN a.content;
                        END IF;
                        l_key := object_key(a);
                        CASE a.storage
                        WHEN 'AWS4_S3_PKG' THEN
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin :r := aws4_s3_pkg.get_object_blob(p_bucket => :b, p_canonical_uri => :k); end;'
                                USING OUT l_blob, required('ARCHIVE_BUCKET'), '/' || l_key;
                        WHEN 'DBMS_CLOUD' THEN
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin :r := dbms_cloud.get_object(credential_name => :c, object_uri => :u); end;'
                                USING OUT l_blob, required('ARCHIVE_CREDENTIAL'), RTRIM(required('ARCHIVE_BASE_URI'), '/') || '/' || l_key;
                        WHEN 'CUSTOM' THEN
                            EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'begin :r := ' || DBMS_ASSERT.QUALIFIED_SQL_NAME(required('ARCHIVE_GET_FUNCTION')) ||
                                              '(p_object_key => :k); end;'
                                USING OUT l_blob, l_key;
                        ELSE
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20043, 'Archive ' || a.archive_id || ' has no file in the database and no remote storage.');
                        END CASE;
                        IF l_blob IS NULL OR DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH(l_blob) = 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20044, 'Archive ' || a.archive_id || ': the file came back empty from ' || a.location || '.');
                        END IF;
                        RETURN l_blob;
                    END;

                    FUNCTION get_file(p_archive_id IN NUMBER) RETURN BLOB IS
                        a util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT * INTO a FROM util_audit_archive_files WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        RETURN fetch_file(a);
                    END;

                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Archive
                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    FUNCTION archive_month(
                        p_table_name IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_month      IN DATE
                    ) RETURN NUMBER IS
                        l_table  VARCHAR2(255) := UPPER(TRIM(p_table_name));
                        l_start  TIMESTAMP     := CAST(TRUNC(p_month, 'MM') AS TIMESTAMP);
                        l_end    TIMESTAMP     := CAST(ADD_MONTHS(TRUNC(p_month, 'MM'), 1) AS TIMESTAMP);
                        l_text   CLOB;
                        l_raw    BLOB;
                        l_gz     BLOB;
                        l_events NUMBER := 0;
                        l_recs   NUMBER;
                        l_busy   NUMBER;
                        l_id     NUMBER;
                        l_dest   INTEGER := 1;
                        l_src    INTEGER := 1;
                        l_ctx    INTEGER := DBMS_LOB.DEFAULT_LANG_CTX;
                        l_warn   INTEGER;
                        l_hash   VARCHAR2(80);
                        l_kind   VARCHAR2(20);
                        l_user   VARCHAR2(255);
                    BEGIN
                        -- One live archive per table and month
                        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO l_busy FROM util_audit_archive_files
                         WHERE table_name = l_table AND period_start = l_start
                           AND status IN ('CREATED', 'STORED', 'PURGED', 'FAILED');
                        IF l_busy > 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20045, l_table || ' ' || TO_CHAR(l_start, 'YYYY-MM') ||
                                ' is already archived. Restore it first to archive it again.');
                        END IF;

                        DBMS_LOB.CREATETEMPORARY(l_text, TRUE);
                        FOR e IN (
                            SELECT JSON_OBJECT(
                                       'transaction_id'    VALUE t.transaction_id,
                                       'db_transaction_id' VALUE t.db_transaction_id,
                                       'table_name'        VALUE t.table_name,
                                       'pk_value'          VALUE t.pk_value_vc,
                                       'transaction_type'  VALUE t.transaction_type,
                                       'username'          VALUE t.username,
                                       'audit_ts'          VALUE t.audit_ts,
                                       'audit_context'     VALUE t.audit_context FORMAT JSON,
                                       'old_row'           VALUE t.old_row_json FORMAT JSON,
                                       'new_row'           VALUE t.new_row_json FORMAT JSON,
                                       'changes'           VALUE (
                                           SELECT JSON_ARRAYAGG(
                                                      JSON_OBJECT(
                                                          'column_name' VALUE r.column_name,
                                                          'data_type'   VALUE r.data_type,
                                                          'old_value'   VALUE r.old_value,
                                                          'new_value'   VALUE r.new_value,
                                                          'old_clob'    VALUE r.old_clob,
                                                          'new_clob'    VALUE r.new_clob,
                                                          'change_hash' VALUE r.change_hash,
                                                          'audit_ts'    VALUE r.audit_ts
                                                          ABSENT ON NULL RETURNING CLOB)
                                                      ORDER BY r.util_audit_record_id RETURNING CLOB)
                                             FROM util_audit_records r
                                            WHERE r.transaction_id = t.transaction_id)
                                       ABSENT ON NULL RETURNING CLOB) AS line
                              FROM util_audit_txn t
                             WHERE t.table_name = l_table
                               AND t.audit_ts >= l_start
                               AND t.audit_ts <  l_end
                             ORDER BY t.audit_ts, t.audit_txn_id
                        ) LOOP
                            DBMS_LOB.APPEND(l_text, e.line);
                            DBMS_LOB.WRITEAPPEND(l_text, 1, CHR(10));
                            l_events := l_events + 1;
                        END LOOP;

                        IF l_events = 0 THEN
                            RETURN NULL;
                        END IF;

                        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO l_recs
                          FROM util_audit_records r
                         WHERE r.transaction_id IN (SELECT t.transaction_id FROM util_audit_txn t
                                                     WHERE t.table_name = l_table AND t.audit_ts >= l_start AND t.audit_ts < l_end);

                        DBMS_LOB.CREATETEMPORARY(l_raw, TRUE);
                        DBMS_LOB.CONVERTTOBLOB(l_raw, l_text, DBMS_LOB.LOBMAXSIZE, l_dest, l_src,
                                               NLS_CHARSET_ID('AL32UTF8'), l_ctx, l_warn);
                        l_gz   := UTL_COMPRESS.LZ_COMPRESS(l_raw);
                        l_hash := sha256(l_gz);
                        l_kind := storage;
                        l_user := NVL(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), USER);

                        INSERT INTO util_audit_archive_files
                            (table_name, period_start, period_end, event_count, record_count, file_bytes, file_sha256,
                             storage, status, content, created_by)
                        VALUES
                            (l_table, l_start, l_end, l_events, l_recs, DBMS_LOB.GETLENGTH(l_gz), l_hash,
                             l_kind, 'CREATED', l_gz, l_user)
                        RETURNING archive_id INTO l_id;

                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files
                           SET file_name = l_table || '_' || TO_CHAR(l_start, 'YYYY-MM', 'NLS_CALENDAR=GREGORIAN') ||
                                           '_' || l_id || '.jsonl.gz'
                         WHERE archive_id = l_id;
                        COMMIT;

                        DBMS_LOB.FREETEMPORARY(l_text);
                        DBMS_LOB.FREETEMPORARY(l_raw);
                        RETURN l_id;
                    END archive_month;

                    PROCEDURE store(p_archive_id IN NUMBER) IS
                        a          util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE;
                        l_location VARCHAR2(1000);
                        l_back     BLOB;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT * INTO a FROM util_audit_archive_files WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id FOR UPDATE;
                        IF a.status NOT IN ('CREATED', 'FAILED') OR a.content IS NULL THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20046, 'Archive ' || p_archive_id || ' is ' || a.status || ', not waiting to be stored.');
                        END IF;
                        -- A retry goes to the storage configured now (the setting may have
                        -- been corrected after a failure)
                        a.storage := storage;
                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files SET storage = a.storage WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        -- Release the row lock: the S3 package can commit on its own
                        COMMIT;

                        BEGIN
                            put_file(a.storage, object_key(a), a.content, l_location);

                            -- Read it back and compare, before the local copy is dropped
                            IF a.storage <> 'DATABASE' THEN
                                a.content := NULL;
                                l_back := fetch_file(a);
                                IF sha256(l_back, a.file_sha256) <> a.file_sha256 THEN
                                    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20047, 'The stored file differs from the archive (SHA-256 mismatch).');
                                END IF;
                            END IF;
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                note(p_archive_id, 'Store failed: ' || SQLERRM);
                                RAISE;
                        END;

                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files
                           SET status    = 'STORED',
                               location  = l_location,
                               stored_on = SYSTIMESTAMP,
                               message   = NULL,
                               content   = CASE WHEN storage = 'DATABASE' THEN content END
                         WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        COMMIT;
                    END store;

                    PROCEDURE purge(p_archive_id IN NUMBER) IS
                        a        util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE;
                        l_events NUMBER;
                        l_recs   NUMBER;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT * INTO a FROM util_audit_archive_files WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id FOR UPDATE;
                        IF a.status <> 'STORED' THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20048, 'Archive ' || p_archive_id || ' is ' || a.status ||
                                '. Only a STORED archive can be purged.');
                        END IF;

                        -- The tables must hold exactly what the file holds; a late or
                        -- restored event would otherwise be deleted without a copy
                        SELECT COUNT(*), NVL(SUM((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM util_audit_records r
                                                   WHERE r.transaction_id = t.transaction_id)), 0)
                          INTO l_events, l_recs
                          FROM util_audit_txn t
                         WHERE t.table_name = a.table_name AND t.audit_ts >= a.period_start AND t.audit_ts < a.period_end;
                        IF l_events <> a.event_count OR l_recs <> a.record_count THEN
                            ROLLBACK;
                            -- Stays STORED: the file is fine, the tables changed
                            note(p_archive_id, p_failed => FALSE, p_message => 'Not purged: the audit tables now hold ' || l_events || ' events and ' || l_recs ||
                                ' changes for this month, the file ' || a.event_count || ' and ' || a.record_count ||
                                '. Restore this archive, then archive the month again.');
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20049, 'Archive ' || p_archive_id || ' does not match the audit tables any more; not purged.');
                        END IF;

                        DELETE FROM util_audit_records
                         WHERE transaction_id IN (SELECT t.transaction_id FROM util_audit_txn t
                                                   WHERE t.table_name = a.table_name
                                                     AND t.audit_ts >= a.period_start AND t.audit_ts < a.period_end);
                        DELETE FROM util_audit_txn
                         WHERE table_name = a.table_name AND audit_ts >= a.period_start AND audit_ts < a.period_end;

                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files SET status = 'PURGED', purged_on = SYSTIMESTAMP, message = NULL
                         WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        COMMIT;
                    END purge;

                    PROCEDURE restore(p_archive_id IN NUMBER) IS
                        a      util_audit_archive_files%ROWTYPE;
                        l_gz   BLOB;
                        l_raw  BLOB;
                        l_text CLOB;
                        l_doc  CLOB;
                        l_ev   NUMBER;
                        l_rec  NUMBER;
                        l_dest INTEGER := 1;
                        l_src  INTEGER := 1;
                        l_ctx  INTEGER := DBMS_LOB.DEFAULT_LANG_CTX;
                        l_warn INTEGER;
                    BEGIN
                        SELECT * INTO a FROM util_audit_archive_files WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        l_gz := fetch_file(a);
                        IF sha256(l_gz, a.file_sha256) <> a.file_sha256 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20047, 'Archive ' || p_archive_id || ': the file differs from the one archived (SHA-256 mismatch).');
                        END IF;

                        l_raw := UTL_COMPRESS.LZ_UNCOMPRESS(l_gz);
                        DBMS_LOB.CREATETEMPORARY(l_text, TRUE);
                        DBMS_LOB.CONVERTTOCLOB(l_text, l_raw, DBMS_LOB.LOBMAXSIZE, l_dest, l_src,
                                               NLS_CHARSET_ID('AL32UTF8'), l_ctx, l_warn);
                        -- JSON lines to one JSON document: a line never contains a raw line
                        -- break (JSON escapes them), so the breaks can become commas
                        l_doc := '{"events":[' || REPLACE(RTRIM(l_text, CHR(10)), CHR(10), ',') || ']}';

                        INSERT INTO util_audit_txn
                            (transaction_id, db_transaction_id, table_name, pk_value_vc, transaction_type,
                             username, audit_context, old_row_json, new_row_json, audit_ts)
                        SELECT j.transaction_id, j.db_transaction_id, j.table_name, j.pk_value, j.transaction_type,
                               j.username, j.audit_context, j.old_row, j.new_row, j.audit_ts
                          FROM JSON_TABLE(l_doc, '$.events[*]'
                                   COLUMNS (transaction_id    VARCHAR2(64)   PATH '$.transaction_id',
                                            db_transaction_id VARCHAR2(100)  PATH '$.db_transaction_id',
                                            table_name        VARCHAR2(255)  PATH '$.table_name',
                                            pk_value          VARCHAR2(4000) PATH '$.pk_value',
                                            transaction_type  VARCHAR2(6)    PATH '$.transaction_type',
                                            username          VARCHAR2(255)  PATH '$.username',
                                            audit_context     CLOB FORMAT JSON PATH '$.audit_context',
                                            old_row           CLOB FORMAT JSON PATH '$.old_row',
                                            new_row           CLOB FORMAT JSON PATH '$.new_row',
                                            audit_ts          TIMESTAMP      PATH '$.audit_ts')) j
                         WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM util_audit_txn x WHERE x.transaction_id = j.transaction_id);
                        l_ev := SQL%ROWCOUNT;

                        -- Changes only for events that have none yet (those just loaded)
                        INSERT INTO util_audit_records
                            (transaction_id, table_name, pk_value_vc, transaction_type, username, column_name, data_type,
                             old_value, new_value, old_clob, new_clob, change_hash, audit_ts)
                        SELECT j.transaction_id, j.table_name, j.pk_value, j.transaction_type, j.username, j.column_name,
                               j.data_type, j.old_value, j.new_value, j.old_clob, j.new_clob, j.change_hash,
                               NVL(j.change_ts, j.audit_ts)
                          FROM JSON_TABLE(l_doc, '$.events[*]'
                                   COLUMNS (transaction_id   VARCHAR2(64)   PATH '$.transaction_id',
                                            table_name       VARCHAR2(255)  PATH '$.table_name',
                                            pk_value         VARCHAR2(4000) PATH '$.pk_value',
                                            transaction_type VARCHAR2(6)    PATH '$.transaction_type',
                                            username         VARCHAR2(255)  PATH '$.username',
                                            audit_ts         TIMESTAMP      PATH '$.audit_ts',
                                            NESTED PATH '$.changes[*]'
                                                COLUMNS (column_name VARCHAR2(255)  PATH '$.column_name',
                                                         data_type   VARCHAR2(128)  PATH '$.data_type',
                                                         old_value   VARCHAR2(4000) PATH '$.old_value',
                                                         new_value   VARCHAR2(4000) PATH '$.new_value',
                                                         old_clob    CLOB           PATH '$.old_clob',
                                                         new_clob    CLOB           PATH '$.new_clob',
                                                         change_hash VARCHAR2(64)   PATH '$.change_hash',
                                                         change_ts   TIMESTAMP      PATH '$.audit_ts'))) j
                         WHERE j.column_name IS NOT NULL
                           AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM util_audit_records r WHERE r.transaction_id = j.transaction_id);
                        l_rec := SQL%ROWCOUNT;

                        UPDATE util_audit_archive_files
                           SET status = 'RESTORED', restored_on = SYSTIMESTAMP,
                               message = 'Loaded ' || l_ev || ' events and ' || l_rec || ' changes.'
                         WHERE archive_id = p_archive_id;
                        COMMIT;
                        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Archive ' || p_archive_id || ': loaded ' || l_ev || ' events and ' || l_rec || ' changes.');
                    END restore;

                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    -- Scheduled work
                    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                    PROCEDURE run(p_max_files IN PLS_INTEGER DEFAULT 100) IS
                        l_keep   NUMBER := NVL(TO_NUMBER(get_setting('ARCHIVE_KEEP_MONTHS')), 12);
                        l_purge  BOOLEAN := NVL(UPPER(get_setting('ARCHIVE_PURGE')), 'N') = 'Y';
                        l_before TIMESTAMP;
                        l_id     NUMBER;
                        l_made   PLS_INTEGER := 0;
                        l_failed PLS_INTEGER := 0;

                        PROCEDURE step(p_what IN VARCHAR2, p_id IN NUMBER) IS
                        BEGIN
                            CASE p_what
                                WHEN 'STORE' THEN store(p_id);
                                WHEN 'PURGE' THEN purge(p_id);
                            END CASE;
                            DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(INITCAP(p_what) || 'd archive ' || p_id);
                        EXCEPTION
                            WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                ROLLBACK;
                                l_failed := l_failed + 1;
                                DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(INITCAP(p_what) || ' of archive ' || p_id || ' failed: ' || SQLERRM);
                        END;
                    BEGIN
                        IF l_keep < 1 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20050, 'ARCHIVE_KEEP_MONTHS must be 1 or more.');
                        END IF;
                        l_before := CAST(ADD_MONTHS(TRUNC(SYSDATE, 'MM'), -l_keep) AS TIMESTAMP);

                        -- 1. Files that were built but not stored (a failed upload, say)
                        FOR a IN (SELECT archive_id FROM util_audit_archive_files
                                   WHERE status IN ('CREATED', 'FAILED') AND content IS NOT NULL
                                   ORDER BY archive_id) LOOP
                            step('STORE', a.archive_id);
                        END LOOP;

                        -- 2. New files: every table and month older than the kept months
                        FOR m IN (
                            SELECT t.table_name, TRUNC(CAST(t.audit_ts AS DATE), 'MM') month_start
                              FROM util_audit_txn t
                             WHERE t.audit_ts < l_before
                             GROUP BY t.table_name, TRUNC(CAST(t.audit_ts AS DATE), 'MM')
                            HAVING NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM util_audit_archive_files a
                                                WHERE a.table_name = t.table_name
                                                  AND a.period_start = CAST(TRUNC(CAST(t.audit_ts AS DATE), 'MM') AS TIMESTAMP)
                                                  AND a.status IN ('CREATED', 'STORED', 'PURGED', 'FAILED'))
                             ORDER BY 2, 1
                        ) LOOP
                            EXIT WHEN l_made >= p_max_files;
                            BEGIN
                                l_id := archive_month(m.table_name, m.month_start);
                                l_made := l_made + 1;
                                DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Archived ' || m.table_name || ' ' || TO_CHAR(m.month_start, 'YYYY-MM') ||
                                                     ' as archive ' || l_id);
                                step('STORE', l_id);
                            EXCEPTION
                                WHEN OTHERS THEN
                                    ROLLBACK;
                                    l_failed := l_failed + 1;
                                    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Archiving ' || m.table_name || ' ' || TO_CHAR(m.month_start, 'YYYY-MM') ||
                                                         ' failed: ' || SQLERRM);
                            END;
                        END LOOP;

                        -- 3. Purge what is safely stored
                        IF l_purge THEN
                            FOR a IN (SELECT archive_id FROM util_audit_archive_files
                                       WHERE status = 'STORED' AND period_end <= l_before ORDER BY archive_id) LOOP
                                step('PURGE', a.archive_id);
                            END LOOP;
                        END IF;

                        IF l_failed > 0 THEN
                            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20051, l_failed || ' archive step(s) failed. See UTIL_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_FILES.MESSAGE.');
                        END IF;
                    END run;

                    PROCEDURE unschedule IS
                    BEGIN
                        DBMS_SCHEDULER.DROP_JOB(c_job, force => TRUE);
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            IF SQLCODE <> -27475 THEN  -- job does not exist
                                RAISE;
                            END IF;
                    END;

                    PROCEDURE schedule(p_repeat_interval IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'FREQ=DAILY;BYHOUR=2;BYMINUTE=0') IS
                    BEGIN
                        unschedule;
                        DBMS_SCHEDULER.CREATE_JOB(
                            job_name        => c_job,
                            job_type        => 'PLSQL_BLOCK',
                            job_action      => 'begin util_audit_archive.run; end;',
                            repeat_interval => p_repeat_interval,
                            enabled         => TRUE,
                            comments        => 'util_audit: archive old audit history (util_audit_archive.run)');
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            IF SQLCODE = -27486 OR SQLCODE = -1031 THEN
                                RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20052, 'Scheduling needs the CREATE JOB privilege: grant create job to ' || $$PLSQL_UNIT_OWNER);
                            END IF;
                            RAISE;
                    END schedule;

                END util_audit_archive;
                /
                -- util_audit install check: every util_audit object must be valid
                DECLARE
                    l_bad VARCHAR2(4000);
                BEGIN
                    SELECT LISTAGG(object_type || ' ' || object_name, ', ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY object_name)
                    INTO l_bad
                    FROM user_objects
                    WHERE status = 'INVALID'
                      AND (object_name LIKE 'UTIL\_AUDIT%' ESCAPE '\' OR object_name LIKE 'V\_UTIL\_AUDIT%' ESCAPE '\')
                      -- migrate_v1.sql rebuilds this one after setup.sql has run
                      AND object_name <> 'V_UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS_V1';
                    IF l_bad IS NOT NULL THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20101, 'util_audit installed with invalid objects: ' || l_bad ||
                            '. Run: select * from user_errors where name like ''%UTIL_AUDIT%''');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                ```
        }
    )

    upgradeScript upgrade-help (
        execution {
            sequence: 150
        }
        script {
            content:
                ```
                -- Help articles (generated from help.sql by tools/sync_supporting_objects.py)
                -- util_audit v1 guard
                DECLARE
                    l_v1 NUMBER;
                BEGIN
                    SELECT COUNT(*)
                      INTO l_v1
                      FROM user_tables t
                     WHERE t.table_name = 'UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS'
                       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_tab_columns c
                                        WHERE c.table_name = t.table_name
                                          AND c.column_name = 'PK_VALUE_VC');
                    IF l_v1 > 0 THEN
                        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                            'This schema has util_audit v1 (UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS without PK_VALUE_VC). ' ||
                            'Installing over it would break the v1 audit triggers, so nothing was changed. ' ||
                            'Run migrate_v1.sql instead (see docs/migrating-from-v1.md).');
                    END IF;
                END;
                /
                ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                -- util_audit in-app help
                --
                -- One UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE row per topic, written in Markdown and rendered
                -- with APEX_MARKDOWN.TO_HTML on the app's Documentation page (page 9).
                -- PAGE_ID links an article to the screen it explains: Help in the top bar
                -- opens page 9 with the current page number, and page 9 shows that article.
                -- ADMIN_ONLY = Y hides an article from users who are not workspace
                -- administrators or developers.
                --
                -- Installed by the Util Audit app's Supporting Objects. Safe to re-run: the
                -- table is created only when missing. A missing article is added. An
                -- article nobody has edited gets the new text; SEED_BODY keeps the text it
                -- was shipped with, so an article edited in the app is never overwritten.
                ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                DECLARE
                    PROCEDURE ddl(p_sql IN VARCHAR2) IS
                    BEGIN
                        EXECUTE IMMEDIATE p_sql;
                    EXCEPTION
                        WHEN OTHERS THEN
                            -- ORA-00955: name already used, ORA-02260/02261: key already exists,
                            -- ORA-01430: column already exists
                            IF SQLCODE NOT IN (-955, -2260, -2261, -1430) THEN
                                RAISE;
                            END IF;
                    END;
                BEGIN
                    ddl(q'[
                create table UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE
                (
                    ID          NUMBER generated by default on null as identity
                        constraint UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_PK
                            primary key,
                    SLUG        VARCHAR2(100)  not null
                        constraint UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_SLUG_UK
                            unique,
                    TITLE       VARCHAR2(200)  not null,
                    PAGE_ID     NUMBER,
                    ADMIN_ONLY  VARCHAR2(1)    default 'N' not null
                        constraint UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_ADM_CK
                            check (admin_only in ('Y', 'N')),
                    SORT_ORDER  NUMBER         default 100 not null,
                    BODY        CLOB,
                    ACTIVE      VARCHAR2(1)    default 'Y' not null
                        constraint UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_ACT_CK
                            check (active in ('Y', 'N')),
                    CREATED     DATE           not null,
                    CREATED_BY  VARCHAR2(255)  not null,
                    UPDATED     DATE           not null,
                    UPDATED_BY  VARCHAR2(255)  not null
                )]');

                    ddl(q'[create index UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_PAGE_IX
                    on UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE (PAGE_ID)]');

                    -- The text the article was shipped with (added later)
                    ddl(q'[alter table UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE add (SEED_BODY CLOB)]');
                END;
                /

                create or replace trigger UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE_BIU
                    before insert or update on UTIL_AUDIT_DOC_ARTICLE
                    for each row
                begin
                    if inserting then
                        :new.created    := sysdate;
                        :new.created_by := nvl(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), user);
                    end if;
                    :new.updated    := sysdate;
                    :new.updated_by := nvl(sys_context('APEX$SESSION', 'APP_USER'), user);
                    :new.slug       := lower(regexp_replace(trim(:new.slug), '[^A-Za-z0-9-]+', '-'));
                end;
                /

                -- Seed articles. Blank lines inside a PL/SQL block are safe in SQL*Plus,
                -- SQLcl and APEX script runs, so the Markdown keeps its paragraphs.
                DECLARE
                    PROCEDURE seed(
                        p_slug       IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_title      IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_page_id    IN NUMBER,
                        p_admin_only IN VARCHAR2,
                        p_sort_order IN NUMBER,
                        p_body       IN CLOB
                    ) IS
                    BEGIN
                        -- Unedited: the body is still the shipped text. Rows from before
                        -- SEED_BODY existed count as unedited if never updated after insert.
                        UPDATE util_audit_doc_article a
                           SET body = p_body, seed_body = p_body
                         WHERE a.slug = p_slug
                           AND (DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(a.body, a.seed_body) = 0
                                OR (a.seed_body IS NULL AND a.updated <= a.created + 2 / 86400)
                                OR DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(a.body, p_body) = 0)
                           -- only when something changes, so a re-run touches nothing
                           AND (NVL(DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(a.body, p_body), 1) <> 0
                                OR NVL(DBMS_LOB.COMPARE(a.seed_body, p_body), 1) <> 0);

                        INSERT INTO util_audit_doc_article (slug, title, page_id, admin_only, sort_order, body, seed_body)
                        SELECT p_slug, p_title, p_page_id, p_admin_only, p_sort_order, p_body, p_body
                        FROM dual
                        WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM util_audit_doc_article WHERE slug = p_slug);
                    END;
                BEGIN
                    seed('getting-started', 'Getting started', NULL, 'N', 10, q'[
                Util Audit records every change to the tables you choose: who changed which row, when, and what each column held before and after. It can also put a row back the way it was.

                ## Who can do what

                | You are | You can |
                | --- | --- |
                | Workspace administrator or developer | Everything: start and stop auditing, restore rows, purge and archive history |
                | Any other workspace user | Look at everything, change nothing |

                ## Finding your way

                The menu at the top has **Home**, **Tables**, **Events**, **Row History**, **Errors**, **Maintenance**, **Archive**, **Query Generator** and **Documentation**. Maintenance and Archive only appear for administrators.

                Press **Help** in the top bar on any screen to open the article for that screen.

                The app follows your computer's light or dark setting. The **Theme** menu in the top bar switches between **Match system**, **Light** and **Dark**, and remembers your choice.

                ## Start in three steps

                1. Open **Tables** and click a table name.
                2. Press **Start Auditing**.
                3. Change a row in that table. The change appears under **Events** straight away.
                ]');

                    seed('home', 'Home', 1, 'N', 20, q'[
                Home shows how much is being recorded.

                ## The four counts

                1. **Audited tables**: tables with an audit trigger, whether paused or not.
                2. **Events (24h)**: inserts, updates and deletes recorded in the last 24 hours.
                3. **Events (7 days)**: the same for the last week.
                4. **Errors (7 days)**: changes the triggers could not record. Anything above 0 is worth a look under **Errors**.

                ## Events per day

                One bar per day for the last 14 days, split into inserts, updates and deletes.

                ## Recent events

                The last 10 changes. Click the time to open the event.
                ]');

                    seed('tables', 'Tables', 2, 'N', 30, q'[
                Tables lists every table in the schema and whether it is audited. Click a table name to open it.

                ## Status

                | Status | Meaning |
                | --- | --- |
                | Auditing | Changes are being recorded |
                | Paused | The trigger is in place but records nothing |
                | Not audited | No audit trigger on this table |
                | Trigger invalid | The trigger does not compile. Open the table and press **Re-create Trigger** |
                | Trigger disabled | Someone disabled the trigger in the database |

                ## Other columns

                - **Ignored Columns**: bookkeeping columns whose changes are not listed.
                - **Excluded Columns**: secrets that are never recorded at all.
                - **Child Tables**: tables that point at this one with a foreign key. **Unaudited Child Tables** counts the ones without a trigger. Restoring a deleted row cannot bring back rows from those.
                - **Events** and **Last Event**: how much has been recorded, and when last.

                A table needs a primary key before it can be audited.
                ]');

                    seed('auditing-a-table', 'Auditing a table', 3, 'N', 35, q'[
                Open **Tables** and click a table name. The panel on the right shows the table's status and what you can do with it. Only administrators see the buttons.

                ## Buttons

                | Button | What it does |
                | --- | --- |
                | **Start Auditing** | Creates the audit trigger. Recording starts at once |
                | **Pause** | Stops recording but keeps the trigger |
                | **Resume** | Starts recording again after a pause |
                | **Re-create Trigger** | Rebuilds the trigger. Do this after adding or dropping columns |
                | **Stop Auditing** | Removes the trigger. The history already recorded is kept |

                ## Ignored columns

                Move the columns you do not want recorded to the right, then press **Save Ignored Columns**. The trigger is rebuilt straight away, and the list is kept every time the trigger is rebuilt.

                A change that only touches ignored columns records nothing. These are always ignored: CREATED, CREATED_ON, CREATED_BY, UPDATED, UPDATED_ON, UPDATED_BY, MODIFIED, MODIFIED_ON, MODIFIED_BY.

                Ignored columns are still kept in the copy of the whole row that each event stores, so a restored row gets them back.

                ## Excluded columns

                For secrets, such as password hashes and reset tokens. An excluded column is never written to the audit trail: not as a change, and not in the copy of the whole row. Key columns cannot be excluded.

                A restored row gets an empty value or the column default for excluded columns. If such a column is required and has no default, a deleted row cannot be restored, and Restore says so.

                Turn on **Also remove them from history already recorded** to delete these columns from everything this table has recorded so far. This cannot be undone, and archive files made earlier keep them.

                ## Child tables

                Lists every table that points at this one, how it reacts when a row here is deleted (**On Delete**), and whether it is audited.

                When you restore a deleted row, Util Audit also brings back its child rows, but only from audited child tables. Audit the child tables too if you want restores to be complete.

                ## Trigger code

                Shows the exact trigger the app creates for this table. Nothing runs when you open it.
                ]');

                    seed('events', 'Events', 4, 'N', 40, q'[
                Events lists every recorded change, newest first.

                ## Finding a change

                - Type in **Search** to match any word in the list.
                - Tick a **Table**, **Type** (INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE) or **User** to narrow the list. The numbers next to each value show how many events match.
                - Enter dates under **When** and press **Go** to limit the time range.

                ## Columns

                **Key** is the row's primary key. A key made of several columns is shown as `{"ORDER_ID":"100","LINE_NO":"1"}`. **Changed Columns** lists the columns that changed. An insert or delete lists every column.

                ## Opening a change

                Click the time to see the full event and, for administrators, to restore the row. Click **History** to see every change to that row.
                ]');

                    seed('event-and-restore', 'An event, and restoring a row', 5, 'N', 50, q'[
                The Event panel shows one recorded change.

                ## What it shows

                - **Event**: when, which table and row, what kind of change, and who made it. The user is the APEX user for changes made in an APEX app, otherwise the database user.
                - **Context**: where the change came from. For an APEX app: the app, page and session numbers and the user's IP address. For other tools: the program name (**Module**), the computer (**Host**) and the operating-system user.
                - **Column Changes**: each column's value before and after.

                ## Restoring a row

                Restore puts the row back the way it was just before this event.

                - For a **delete**, the row is inserted again.
                - For an **update**, the columns go back to their old values.
                - An **insert** cannot be restored.

                1. Leave **Include child rows** on to also bring back rows in audited child tables that were deleted, or had their link cleared, in the same transaction.
                2. Press **Preview Restore**. The restore runs, the **Result** box lists every row it would touch, and then everything is rolled back. Nothing changes.
                3. If the result looks right, press **Restore**.

                If the row changed again after this event, Restore stops and says so. Turn on **Overwrite later changes** to restore anyway. Those later changes are then lost.

                If any step fails, nothing is changed. The reason appears in **Result**.

                The restore is recorded like any other change. Its events show `util_audit.restore_row` as the **Action** in their context.

                ## What a restore cannot bring back

                - Columns of unsupported types, such as BLOB. A re-inserted row gets an empty value or the column default for those.
                - Events copied from util_audit v1. They have no copy of the whole row.
                - Rows in child tables that are not audited. The Result says which tables these are.
                - A row whose primary key is GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, after a delete.
                ]');

                    seed('row-history', 'Row History', 6, 'N', 60, q'[
                Row History shows every recorded change to one row.

                1. Choose the **Table**.
                2. Choose the row's **Key**. The list shows every key that has events.

                The **Timeline** lists the changes, newest first. Click one to open the event. **All Column Changes** lists each column's old and new value, change by change. Long values are cut at 200 characters here; open the event to see them in full.

                Opening a change from **Events** with **History** fills in the table and key for you.

                If a change altered the primary key, the history before and after it sits under two different keys.
                ]');

                    seed('errors', 'Errors', 7, 'N', 70, q'[
                When a trigger cannot record a change, the change itself still goes through. The failure is recorded here instead, so nothing is lost without a trace.

                Each row shows when it happened, the table, the kind of change, the row's key, the user, and the error with the exact line it came from (**Backtrace**).

                ## What to do

                - A single error: check the message. It usually names the cause, for example a value too large for a column.
                - Many errors on one table after a change to that table: open the table under **Tables** and press **Re-create Trigger**.

                Old errors can be deleted under **Maintenance**.
                ]');

                    seed('maintenance', 'Maintenance', 8, 'Y', 80, q'[
                Maintenance is for administrators.

                ## Purge Audit History

                Deletes events, and their column changes, recorded before the date you choose. Choose a table to purge only that table. Deleted history cannot be restored, and rows cannot be restored from it.

                To remove old history but keep a copy you can load back, use **Archive** instead.

                ## Purge Errors

                Deletes logged errors recorded before the date you choose.

                ## Re-create All Triggers

                Rebuilds every audit trigger from the current code. Do this after upgrading Util Audit, or after adding or dropping columns on several audited tables. The **Result** box lists each table and any that failed.
                ]');

                    seed('how-auditing-works', 'How auditing works', NULL, 'N', 90, q'[
                Each audited table has a trigger that runs after every insert, update and delete, once per row.

                ## What is recorded

                - One **event** per changed row: when, who, the kind of change, the row's key, and the whole row before and after.
                - One **column change** per changed column, with the old and new value. For an insert or a delete, every column that has a value.

                An update that changes nothing, or only ignored columns, records nothing.

                ## Supported column types

                NUMBER, FLOAT, BINARY_FLOAT, BINARY_DOUBLE, VARCHAR2, CHAR, NVARCHAR2, NCHAR, DATE, TIMESTAMP (with or without time zone), INTERVAL, CLOB and RAW (stored as hex). Other types, such as BLOB, are skipped.

                Numbers and dates are always written the same way, whatever the user's language settings: `1234.5` and `2026-02-03T00:00:00`.

                ## Keys

                A table needs a primary key. A key of one column is stored as its value, for example `42`. A key of several columns is stored as `{"ORDER_ID":"100","LINE_NO":"1"}`.

                ## Transactions

                Audit records are part of the same transaction as the change. If the change is rolled back, so is its record.

                ## Speed

                Every audited change does extra work. Audit the tables that matter, and avoid staging tables, bulk loads and high-volume logging tables.
                ]');

                    seed('installing-and-upgrading', 'Installing and upgrading', NULL, 'Y', 100, q'[
                ## Installing

                1. In App Builder, import the Util Audit app into the workspace.
                2. Answer **Yes** to **Install Supporting Objects**. This creates the Util Audit tables, views and packages, and these help articles, in the workspace's schema.

                ## Upgrading

                Import the new version over the old one and install its Supporting Objects again. Your audit history, settings and edited help articles are kept. Then open **Maintenance** and press **Re-create All Triggers** so every table uses the new trigger code.

                ## Schemas that have util_audit v1

                If the schema already runs the older util_audit v1 (a UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS table with a PK_VALUE column), installing stops with an error and changes nothing. Migrate the schema first with `migrate_v1.sql` from the util_audit repository, as described in its `docs/migrating-from-v1.md`, then install the app. The v1 history is kept, and the app shows it once it is copied.

                ## Removing

                Delete the app in App Builder and choose to deinstall its Supporting Objects. This removes the triggers, packages, views, tables and the archive job, **including all audit history**. Export anything you need first. Archive files already in S3 stay there.
                ]');

                    seed('query-generator', 'Query Generator', 11, 'N', 105, q'[
                The Query Generator builds an **Audit History** region for a page in another app: the changes recorded for the row that page shows.

                ## Building a region

                1. Choose the **Table** your page shows or edits.
                2. Enter the **Page number in your app**. The key items are named after it, for example `P10_EMP_ID`. If your items have other names, enter them in **Key page items** instead, one per key column, in key column order.
                3. Choose what to **Show**:
                    - **One row per changed column**: each column's old and new value.
                    - **One row per change**: one line per insert, update or delete, listing the columns that changed.
                4. Optional: pick **Only these columns**, and choose **Include child tables** to also show changes to rows that point at this one, for example an employee's tasks.
                5. Press **Generate**.

                ## Three ways to add it to your app

                - **Audit History plugin**, the easiest. Add the plugin to your app once, then add a region of type Audit History and set Table and Key Items. APEXlang apps can paste the generated block.
                - **SQL for App Builder**: create a Classic Report (or any report) region and paste the SQL. It reads `util_audit_query.history`, so it keeps working as util_audit improves. Turn on **Plain SQL** for a query that calls no package.
                - **APEXlang Region**: a complete Classic Report region to paste into a page's `.apx` file.

                **Preview** shows what the region will display for a row that already has changes.

                ## From SQL

                The same history is available anywhere:

                `select * from table(util_audit_query.history('EMP', :P10_EMP_ID))`

                Give one key value per key column (`p_key1`, `p_key2`, ...). Optional: `p_style => 'EVENTS'`, `p_columns`, `p_child_tables`, `p_max_rows`.

                ## If your app uses another schema

                Enter the util_audit schema in **util_audit schema**, and grant your app's schema EXECUTE on UTIL_AUDIT_QUERY. For plain SQL, grant SELECT on V_UTIL_AUDIT_ROW_HISTORY, V_UTIL_AUDIT_EVENTS and UTIL_AUDIT_RECORDS instead.

                ## Keys

                Keys are matched as text, so a key item must hold the value exactly as stored, for example `100`, not `100.0`.
                ]');

                    seed('archive', 'Archive', 12, 'Y', 85, q'[
                Moves old audit history out of the audit tables into files, preferably in Amazon S3, and brings it back when needed.

                ## How it works

                Each file holds one table's events for one calendar month, as gzipped JSON lines. Every archive goes through these steps:

                1. **Archive**: the file is built.
                2. **Store**: the file is sent to its storage, then read back and compared, so a damaged upload is never counted as stored.
                3. **Purge** (only if you turn it on): the month's events are deleted from the audit tables, after checking that they still match the file.
                4. **Restore** (when needed): the month's events are loaded back. Loading twice does no harm.

                ## Storage and retention

                | Storage | Where the files go |
                |---|---|
                | Database | Kept in the archive table itself |
                | Amazon S3 via AWS4_S3_PKG | Your bucket, through the S3 package this schema already uses for documents |
                | Object storage via DBMS_CLOUD | Needs a DBMS_CLOUD credential and a base URI |
                | Custom procedure | Your own procedure and function, for any other system |

                **Months to keep** says how many recent months stay in the audit tables; older complete months are archived. **Delete archived months** is off at first, so the first runs only make copies. Turn it on once you have restored one archive and checked it.

                ## Schedule

                **Schedule** creates a database job that archives every night (it needs the CREATE JOB privilege). **Run Now** does the same work straight away. The last run's result shows here; a failed step says why in the file list.

                ## Archive files

                One row per file, with its status: Created, Stored, Purged, Restored or Failed. You can store a file again after a failure, purge it, restore it, or download it.

                A restored month is archived again by the next scheduled run. To keep it in the tables for a while, stop the schedule or raise **Months to keep**.
                ]');

